Fuminori: "Why, Saya? Why do you go so far for me?"

173
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Saya: "Fuminori..."

174
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:15,000
Fuminori: "I don't understand it... I don't, but I'm losing myself to you more every day. I can't live without you, Saya."

175
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:22,000
*I wrap my arms tighter around her, praying that our bodies will melt together and never again be apart.*

176
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:28,000
Fuminori: "Tell me, please. What must I do to keep you with me? How can I repay you?"

177
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Saya: "Keep holding me," Saya whispers into my chest. "I want you to make love to me. I want to stay like this forever. I won't leave you, Fuminori."

178
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Fuminori: "Why? Why me?"

179
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:47,000
Saya: "Because you're all alone," she says softly, gazing up into my eyes. "All alone... just like me."

180
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:57,000
*The sorrow in her voice resonates with my own. There is a deep loneliness in her eyes, a loneliness from which now springs boundless affection.*

181
00:19:57,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Saya: "You're all I have. In the whole wide world, only you will embrace me... my precious Fuminori."

182
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,000
*Now I know.*

183
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:10,000
*No matter what horrors this world unleashes upon me, all I'll ever need is Saya.*

184
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:14,000
*Dr. Tanbo Ryoko has never had a more troublesome patient.*

185
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Ryoko: "Has there been any change since your last visit, Mr. Sakisaka?"

186
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
Fuminori: "No, nothing to speak of."

187
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:29,000
*His voice is hard and flat, his words tossed carelessly into the air. It's like he's speaking to himself in an empty room.*

188
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:38,000
*Ryoko is a surgeon, not a psychiatrist, but even she can sense the thickness of the wall he has erected between himself and the world.*

189
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Ryoko: "Any nausea, dizziness, or hallucinations?"

190
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Fuminori: "No."

191
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:58,000
*While Sakisaka appears to be looking at Ryoko, his gaze is actually aimed a fraction down and to the side. He's only superficially engaged in the conversation, when in truth it does not interest him in the slightest -- perfect rejection.*

192
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:04,000
*Realizing that she can't interview him like this, Ryoko sighs and sets her chart aside.*

193
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:14,000
Ryoko: "Mr. Sakisaka. The procedure you received at this hospital was the latest in experimental neurosurgery. We explained this before, didn't we?"

194
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:31,000
*Treatment of subdural hematoma through the use of micromachines, a procedure available in Japan exclusively here at the T University Medical Center, had been the only way to save Sakisaka Fuminori from a cerebral contusion that should have been fatal.*

195
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:37,000
Ryoko: "With any experimental treatment, there is always the risk of unexpected complications."

196
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,000
Fuminori: "Of course."

197
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:48,000
*Sakisaka Fuminori's lips twist slightly in what might be a bitter -- or mocking -- smile, but it is gone before Ryoko can discern its meaning.*

198
00:21:48,000 --> 00:22:01,000
Ryoko: "Normally, I would never say anything to frighten a patient... but there have been reports of serious neurological disorders post-surgery. We must continue to monitor your condition carefully."

199
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:07,000
*Hence these weekly check-ups. If only he would take them a little more seriously.*

200
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:13,000
Fuminori: "How was last week's MRI?" Sakisaka asks abruptly, as if to catch Ryoko off guard.

201
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:27,000
*MRI -- Magnetic Resonance Imaging -- is a way for doctors to examine the brain in detail without opening the patient's skull. Surprised by Sakisaka's uncommon technical knowledge, Ryoko recalls his profile.*

202
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:31,000
Ryoko: "Oh, that's right. You're a medical student, aren't you?"

203
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:38,000
Fuminori: "The kind of anomaly you're worried about should show up on the MRI, right? Did you find anything?"

204
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:39,000
Ryoko: "......No."

205
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:50,000
*There was nothing -- not the slightest hint of abnormal activity. For a procedure with such a low rate of success, the results have been nothing short of miraculous.*

206
00:22:50,000 --> 00:23:01,000
*However, something still bothers Ryoko. She can't shake the feeling that he's hiding something beneath his guarded exterior -- some terrible weight on his soul, perhaps.*

207
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:08,000
*But if it is an inorganic problem, then there's nothing she can do as long as he refuses to explain it.*

208
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:16,000
Fuminori: "I'm fine, doctor. I've lived on my own for three months without any problems. What could go wrong now?"

209
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:25,000
Ryoko: "Please, you know that continued observation is required after these difficult surgeries. You have to trust us a little more."

210
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:32,000
Fuminori: "I suppose you're right. I do want to trust you, Doctor. Can I come to you with anything?"

211
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:41,000
Ryoko: "Yes, of course," Ryoko answers, smiling to cover up her irritation. Sakisaka asked exactly the same question during last week's visit.

212
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:47,000
Fuminori: "Well then, let's pick up where we left off. Have you learned anything about Dr. Ogai?"

213
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:48,000
Ryoko: "......"

214
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:52,000
*Unable to answer, Ryoko hardens the mask of her smile.*

215
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:58,000
*As before, the patient is inquiring about someone whom he has no business knowing.*

216
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:04,000
Ryoko: "If you don't mind my asking, what does Dr. Ogai have to do with your treatment?"

217
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:09,000
Fuminori: "You just told me to trust you, and now you're keeping secrets?"

218
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:20,000
*Ryoko is used to patients treating her with hostility. After all, some degree of paranoia is natural when dealing with someone who holds your life in her hands.*

219
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:32,000
*In Sakisaka, however, she doesn't see the shortsighted impatience that other patients exhibit. His demeanor is perfectly calm, almost like a detective questioning a suspect.*

220
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:38,000
Ryoko: "He left this hospital some time ago. I never had any contact with him myself."

221
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:40,000
Fuminori: "Do you know why he left?"

222
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:52,000
Ryoko: "Yes, I believe it was personal," Ryoko answers smoothly, her earlier hesitation gone. Having decided at the outset to lie, she has no trouble doing so with a straight face.

223
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:57,000
Ryoko: "But why do you keep asking about Dr. Ogai? Do you know him?"

224
00:24:57,000 --> 00:25:01,000
Fuminori: "Did you know that the doctor has gone missing?"

225
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:02,000
Ryoko: "No."

226
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:09,000
*Ryoko realizes that her answer may have been a little too quick. She should have acted more surprised.*

227
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:16,000
Fuminori: "I've recently become close with a relative of his. It was she who asked me to find him."

228
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:19,000
*A relative? Ryoko considers this with a frown.*

229
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:22,000
Ryoko: "I didn't think Dr. Ogai had any relatives."

230
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:24,000
Fuminori: "Oh, who told you that?"

231
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:32,000
Ryoko: "I... heard it from a nurse," Ryoko replies, remembering that she just claimed to have had no contact with the man.

232
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:37,000
Fuminori: "I see. So the doctor was famous enough for nurses to gossip about him?"

233
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:40,000
Ryoko: "He was an unusual man, I hear."

234
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:44,000
Fuminori: "But no one knows why he left the university?"

235
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:45,000
Ryoko: "......"

236
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:51,000
*Ryoko falls silent, knowing that this isn't a topic she can brush away with a smile.*

237
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:58,000
*Sakisaka seems to have finally grasped her mood, however, as his strangely stiff tone softens a little.*

238
00:25:58,000 --> 00:26:05,000
Fuminori: "Doctor, I absolutely must find Dr. Ogai. There's a girl who's lost without him. Can't you help me?"

239
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:09,000
Ryoko: "Isn't this something the police should handle?"

240
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:28,000
*Although she makes it sound like the most obvious thing in the world, the suggestion is actually a risky gamble. If Ogai Masahiko's disappearance becomes a police matter, then the university will be investigated. Everyone who was involved in the incident will be at risk of exposure.*

241
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:31,000
*And of course, that includes Ryoko herself.*

242
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:48,000
*She knows, however, that Sakisaka is unlikely to go to the police. First of all, his excuse is obviously a lie. They already made sure that Ogai had no relatives who might come looking for him, which is why they could bury the truth of what happened.*

243
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:52,000
*But then how did Sakisaka, a mere patient, learn about Ogai?*

244
00:26:52,000 --> 00:27:02,000
Ryoko: "I'd be happy to help, but there's been no word from Dr. Ogai since he resigned last April. I can only assume that he's gone on an extended vacation."

245
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:04,000
Fuminori: "......I see."

246
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:09,000
*Expecting resistance, Ryoko is surprised when Sakisaka backs down.*

247
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:18,000
*She's still worried about his condition. And the mysterious link between him and Ogai Masahiko is only making her more uneasy.*

248
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:28,000
*But as long as he doesn't open up to her, there's nothing she can do. After a brief pause, Ryoko writes "progress good" on Sakisaka's chart for today.*

249
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:33,000
Ryoko: "About next week's appointment. How does four o'clock again sou--"

250
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:36,000
*Before she can finish, Sakisaka is gone.*

251
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:39,000
*Yoh is determined to talk to him today.*

252
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:45,000
*Nothing will happen as long as she hesitates. It will only prolong her suffering.*

253
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:48,000
*The time has come to show courage once again.*

254
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:54,000
*Yoh's fourth period on Thursdays is biology. This is her one chance to see Fuminori.*

255
00:27:54,000 --> 00:28:09,000
*As a required course with many students, the lecture is held in a large hall that can seat well over two hundred. But since the room is usually only half full, it is rarely difficult for Yoh to find the seat she wants.*

256
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:19,000
*Yoh prefers to sit near the center, where it is easiest to hear the professor. Most of the students congregate in this area for the same reason.*

257
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:32,000
*Fuminori usually sits beside her, although given the ambiguous state of their relationship, she knows better than to take this for granted. Still, she tries to save a seat whenever possible.*

258
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:40,000
*The classroom isn't crowded today, so Yoh is able to set her bag on the seat next to her without inconveniencing anyone.*

259
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:47,000
*But when the professor arrives at the usual time to start class, there is still no sign of Fuminori.*

260
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:52,000
*After waiting for about ten minutes, Yoh scans the room furtively.*

261
00:28:52,000 --> 00:29:05,000
*Fuminori is there, sitting alone in the far back corner. Did he miss Yoh when he came in? No, he couldn't have. And besides, no serious student would willingly sit so far away from the front.*

262
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:09,000
*Feeling miserable, Yoh slides her bag back over to herself.*

263
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:17,000
*Fuminori is out the door the moment class ends. Yoh barely manages to catch up to him before he disappears down the hallway.*

264
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:18,000
Yoh: "Fuminori!"

265
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:24,000
*Fuminori jerks at the sound of his name. You would think she just screamed at him.*

266
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:28,000
Fuminori: "What?" he turns to her and asks reluctantly.

267
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:47,000
*Now that they are face to face, Yoh is painfully aware of how much weight Fuminori has lost. His sunken eyes and protruding cheekbones are a far cry from the features familiar to her. She wonders whether he's under a lot of stress, or perhaps not getting enough nutrition. Maybe it's both.*

268
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:59,000
*He definitely looks more tense than he should -- afraid, even, though of what she can't imagine. His eyes move restlessly from point to point, and he refuses to look Yoh in the eye.*

269
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:04,000
*It hurts to see Fuminori this way. What could have changed him so?*

270
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:09,000
*Today, she reminds herself, rekindling the flame of courage in her heart.*

271
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:14,000
Yoh: "Um, I want to talk to you about something. Do you have some time?"

272
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:20,000
*The courtyard is empty and silent. No one is willing to sit and chat in the cold November air.*

273
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:22,000
Fuminori: "So what is it?"

274
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:24,000
*((Don't you remember!?))*

275
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:29,000
*Yoh almost blurts the question, but manages to keep her composure.*

276
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:33,000
Yoh: "You've been acting strange lately. I'm worried about you."

277
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:35,000
Fuminori: "Well, a lot's happened."

278
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:40,000
*He smiles like it's nothing, but even that seems stiff and forced.*

279
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:45,000
*He's even standing precisely one pace farther away from her than he used to.*

280
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:47,000
Yoh: "Is that really all?"

281
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:49,000
Fuminori: "What more do you want?"

282
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:53,000
*Yoh manages to keep from flinching at the harshness of his tone.*

283
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:56,000
Yoh: "It's like you're struggling with something."

284
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:57,000
Fuminori: "......"

285
00:30:57,000 --> 00:31:08,000
*Rather than answer, Fuminori grinds his toe into the dead grass at his feet. Fearing that her determination might flag, Yoh lets the words come as they may.*

286
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:16,000
Yoh: "It's like there's a terrible weight on your shoulders, and it's slowly breaking you. That's how you look to me."

287
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:28,000
Fuminori: "Oh really," Fuminori mutters through clenched teeth, no longer trying to deny it or change the topic. This is an even clearer signal of rejection than his prior evasiveness.

288
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:33,000
*But Yoh's determination is strong. Today, at least, she won't back down.*

289
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:42,000
Yoh: "It's times like these," she implores, trying to convey the sincerity of her feelings for him, "that you need your friends."

290
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:48,000
Yoh:  YOur PareNTs. BUt yoU'RE Not aLONE. you HAve KoJi, aND OMi, anD... you HAVe ME."

291
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:59,000
*Yoh can no longer stop the words pouring from her lips. She fears that if she does not unleash the feelings pent-up inside of her, they will be lost forever.*

292
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:03,000
Yoh:  YOu DoN'T hAVe To DEal wITh IT alL bY YOuRSELf."

293
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:07,000
Yoh:  aNYthIng, juST TALking To Us mIGht makE you FEel bETTer."

294
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:09,000
Yoh:  DO! SO plEAse, teLL M--"

295
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:13,000
Fuminori: "Stop it!" Fuminori shouts, silencing Yoh's entreaty.

296
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:21,000
*She promised herself that she wouldn't back down, but Fuminori's expression is terrible enough to shatter her resolve.*

297
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:28,000
*The look in his eyes is not anger, or any other warm-blooded emotion. It is hate -- murderously cold hate.*

298
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:32,000
Fuminori: "Come to think of it, I never gave you an answer, did I?"

299
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:33,000
*He remembers.*

300
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:37,000
*He remembers, yet still he has treated her so coldly.*

301
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:43,000
*That is all the answer she needs. If his words stab any deeper, she might very well die.*

302
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:53,000
Fuminori: "I never saw you in any special way before. When you asked me out, I wasn't sure how to respond. I didn't know how I really felt about you then."

303
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:54,000
Yoh: "Fuminori..."

304
00:32:54,000 --> 00:33:04,000
Fuminori: "But now I can give you an answer. I've had plenty of time to think it over, you know. I hate you, Tsukuba. I don't even want to look at you."

305
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:10,000
*Don't cry, Yoh tells herself, but too late to stop the tears pouring from her eyes.*

306
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:22,000
Fuminori: "I suppose it's too much to hope I never see you again. We do go the same school. So just make this the last time you speak to me, okay? Your voice makes me sick."

307
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:30,000
Yoh: "How can you be so cruel?" Yoh whispers in shock and despair, to which Fuminori twists his lips into a malevolent smile.

308
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:43,000
Fuminori: "You should really try thinking for yourself once in a while. I bet you were just egged on by Omi and Koji, weren't you? Well, you can play at love all you want, but leave me out of it."

309
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:45,000
*That's all Yoh can take.*

310
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:55,000
*Even after shedding tears in front of him, she absolutely refuses to let him hear her cry. Any disgrace would be preferable to breaking down here.*

311
00:33:55,000 --> 00:34:01,000
*So she runs, fleeing breathlessly from the courtyard with Fuminori's cold smile at her back.*

312
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:15,000
*Omi was the first to catch sight of Yoh and Fuminori leaving for the courtyard. Reluctant to interrupt them, but still unwilling to leave them alone, Koji and Omi ended up watching the whole thing from the shadows.*

313
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:17,000
Oumi: "That asshole..."

314
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:31,000
*Throughout the exchange, Omi was clearly itching to jump out and punch Fuminori in the face. Knowing her temper, Koji kept firm hold of her arm until the end. If he hadn't, she might very well have done it.*

315
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:43,000
*Fuminori leaves after Yoh, his every step seeming to take an act of willpower. Koji sighs heavily into the once more empty courtyard, but the bitter taste in his mouth will not go away.*

316
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:45,000
Koji: "What's wrong with him?"

317
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:53,000
*Even Koji cannot forgive Fuminori's treatment of Yoh. However, the first thing that he feels is confusion, not anger.*

318
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:59,000
*Koji has known Fuminori since long before college. Fuminori was never this cruel before.*

319
00:34:59,000 --> 00:35:03,000
*There is no question now that the accident changed him.*

320
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Oumi: "Are you just gonna let this go, Koji?"

321
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:09,000
Koji: "I don't want to, but what can we do?"

322
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:14,000
Oumi: "Something besides watch!" Omi shouts, her face red with fury.

323
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Oumi: "I won't be satisfied until I give him a piece of my mind."

324
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:21,000
Koji: "That won't make Tsukuba feel better."

325
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:24,000
Oumi: "But it'll make me feel better!"

326
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:36,000
*Yoh and Omi are best friends, just like Koji and Fuminori. In fact, it was the relationship between Koji and Omi that brought the other two together. Omi's anger is only natural.*

327
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:40,000
Oumi: "I'm going to talk to him alone. You don't have to come."

328
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:41,000
Koji: "You serious?"

329
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:50,000
Oumi: "Take care of Yoh for me, will you? She's probably really hurt. She'll need someone to be nice to her after she's done crying."

330
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:53,000
Koji: "Wait, shouldn't we switch jobs?"

331
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:58,000
Oumi: "You know how I am. If I try to comfort her, I'll end up making it worse."

332
00:35:58,000 --> 00:36:00,000
Koji: "Yeah, you've got a point."

333
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:01,000
Oumi: "Hey!"

334
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:03,000
Koji: "Anyway, just go easy. Okay?"

335
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:09,000
*Ending the conversation before Omi's mood gets any worse, Koji heads off to find Yoh.*

336
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:14,000
*I feel awful, miserable -- but also refreshed. I've finally crossed the line.*

337
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:29,000
*I knew it would come crashing down like this sooner or later. Having become unable to feel anything but disgust for other people, there was no way I could hope to maintain the relationships I'd had before the accident.*

338
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:47,000
*Today's incident will definitely get back to Koji and Omi, and everyone will be convinced I've had a major change of character. Honestly, I don't care any more. At least I probably won't be committed for this. I just need to avoid acting any stranger than I already have.*

339
00:36:47,000 --> 00:37:04,000
*If this puts a rift between me and the others, good. The thought of all the stress I'll avoid brings a smile to my lips. I'm fed up with them sticking their noses into my life. It's like they don't care that they make my gut turn just by being near me.*

340
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:16,000
*I've been terrified of them until now, but today I struck fear into one of them. In that sense, it's something of a relief... but I'm not entirely without remorse for what happened.*

341
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:33,000
*The person I just demolished with the verbal equivalent of a nuclear bomb used to be my friend Yoh. Even if my senses don't believe it, my mind accepts the theory. I don't have any particular grudge against Yoh herself, and I didn't want to hurt her.*

342
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:37,000
*In retrospect, perhaps I should have just ignored her outright.*

343
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:57,000
*Yoh was an attractive girl. I certainly didn't think badly of her. To be honest, though, I was annoyed when Koji and Omi tried to stick us together. It felt like they were toying with me, and Yoh seemed totally oblivious to the fact that she was dancing to their tune. Her cluelessness was irritating.*

344
00:37:57,000 --> 00:38:13,000
*Still, I knew that none of them meant any harm. Back then, I didn't have any reason to hurt others just to get my way. If having a casual relationship with Yoh would keep our circle of friends together, I was willing to make that compromise.*

345
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:24,000
*Now, however, there is no room in my heart for such forbearance. If merely talking to someone is an ordeal, then how can I be expected to show them kindness?*

346
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:37,000
*These ruminations have left me exhausted. I want to return to Saya as soon as possible, but thinking about the packed trains and crowded downtown streets between here and home saps my spirit.*

347
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:50,000
*Catching sight of a nearby bench, I sit down and close my eyes to the horrors of the world. I can't do anything about the stink or the noise, but at least I can calm my nerves enough to rest.*

348
00:38:50,000 --> 00:39:06,000
*When I regained consciousness in the T University hospital ward, the world was as dark as it is now. I had not yet recovered my sight, even though my eyes and optical nerves were undamaged. It must have been an aftereffect of the accident.*

349
00:39:06,000 --> 00:39:17,000
*Blindness was a shock, but now I know that my suffering then was nothing. After all, my senses of hearing, touch, taste, and smell were all fine at the time.*

350
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:20,000
*The real horror began when my sight returned.*

351
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:28,000
*The one small mercy was that I was able to come to terms with the accident and my neurosurgery while still blind.*

352
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:37,000
*I panicked when I first saw the nightmarish hospital and the bloodcurdling shapes of the doctors and nurses, but I soon guessed the cause.*

353
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:51,000
*It chills me to think of what might have happened if I had recovered my sight along with my consciousness. Suddenly awakening in what can only be described as hell, I would no doubt have lost my mind instantly.*

354
00:39:51,000 --> 00:40:01,000
*Soon my disorder spread to the senses of touch, taste, and smell. As it turns out, sight exerts tremendous influence over the other four senses.*

355
00:40:01,000 --> 00:40:11,000
*The taste of my food, the feel of my bedsheets, the fragrance of my get-well flowers -- all became as unbearably foul as my eyes said they should be.*

356
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:22,000
*Eventually, when even the doctors' voices became unrecognizable as human, I decided to kill myself. I didn't believe for a second that I could live in this new world.*

357
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:24,000
*At least, not until I met Saya.*

358
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:30,000
*One night while thinking of a painless way to die, I found myself succumbing to sleep.*

359
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:37,000
*Drifting between the nightmares in my dreams and the nightmare of reality, I didn't notice her enter my room.*

360
00:40:37,000 --> 00:41:00,000
*The next thing I knew, there was a face staring down at me from next to my bed. The face was not covered in pus, or slime, or earthworm-like feelers. It had smooth white cheeks, round eyes, a lovely little nose -- all things I had never expected to see again. The face was that of a girl, undeniably human and positively glowing with beauty.*

361
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:07,000
Fuminori: "Ahh..." I sighed in admiration, savoring the first peace and joy since regaining my sight.

362
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:10,000
*She had not expected such a reaction, apparently.*

363
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:25,000
Saya: "Aren't you afraid of me?" she asked. Looking at the clock, I saw that it was exactly three in the morning -- no time for a young girl to be alone in the hospital. Perhaps she expected me to mistake her for a ghost.

364
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:31,000
*But I would not have cared if she had been a ghost. Either way, she was a godsend.*

365
00:41:31,000 --> 00:41:34,000
Fuminori: "Who are you? What are you doing here?"

366
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:37,000
Saya: "I'm Saya. I'm looking for my dad."

367
00:41:37,000 --> 00:41:48,000
*I assumed that she was the daughter of a late-shift doctor or another patient. It was unusual, but not unthinkable for such a girl to be wandering around the hospital.*

368
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:51,000
Saya: "It's no fun if you're not scared."

369
00:41:51,000 --> 00:42:01,000
Fuminori: "Wait!" I cried, desperate to keep her from leaving. It was only after she turned around that I realized I hadn't thought of what to say next.

370
00:42:01,000 --> 00:42:02,000
Saya: "Well?"

371
00:42:02,000 --> 00:42:12,000
*Her beautiful eyes drew me in, healing my soul to its core. Through the white haze clouding my mind, I struggled to form a coherent sentence.*

372
00:42:12,000 --> 00:42:17,000
Fuminori: "I shouldn't do this to a girl, but you're the only one I can ask."

373
00:42:17,000 --> 00:42:22,000
*No longer concerned with propriety, I let the words come as they willed.*

374
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:25,000
Fuminori: "Will you let me hold your hand?"

375
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:34,000
*Saya looked confused at first, but then she smiled like she'd just found a new toy. Her smile was brighter than my memories of the sun.*

376
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:42,000
Saya: "You're strange," she said, holding out her slender white hand. "No one's asked me anything like that before."

377
00:42:42,000 --> 00:42:47,000
*Ever so carefully, as though catching snowflakes, I placed my palm against hers.*

378
00:42:47,000 --> 00:42:55,000
*I could feel her human warmth and the softness of her delicate fingers. She was there, just beyond the palm of my hand.*

379
00:42:55,000 --> 00:43:02,000
*Thinking back on the joyful tears I shed then, I know that this is the moment I was saved from my fate.*

380
00:43:02,000 --> 00:43:08,000
Fuminori: "This is the first time in weeks that I've touched someone and felt them as human."

381
00:43:08,000 --> 00:43:09,000
Saya: "......?"

382
00:43:09,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Fuminori: "I can't touch anyone else. I was in an accident, and as a side effect of the surgery, I can't see people as human anymore."

383
00:43:18,000 --> 00:43:20,000
Saya: "Hmm... how mysterious."

384
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:25,000
Saya: "You're interesting," she said, winding her fingers gently around mine.

385
00:43:25,000 --> 00:43:28,000
Fuminori: "Yes, of course! But isn't it dangerous?"

386
00:43:28,000 --> 00:43:32,000
Saya: "Don't worry," she replied. "The night belongs to me."

387
00:43:32,000 --> 00:43:34,000
*And so our rendezvous began.*

388
00:43:34,000 --> 00:43:41,000
*Saya came to my room every night at three a.m., skillfully taking advantage of the duty nurse's shift-change.*

389
00:43:41,000 --> 00:43:46,000
*I was astonished to learn that she was living inside the hospital.*

390
00:43:46,000 --> 00:43:54,000
Saya: "It's so big that I never run out of places to hide," she said, answering my surprise with a nonchalant smile.

391
00:43:54,000 --> 00:44:02,000
*She had been living in the suburbs with her father, she told me, until one day he'd suddenly stopped coming home.*

392
00:44:02,000 --> 00:44:16,000
*After she had tired of waiting for his return, Saya had decided one night to sneak into the hospital where he'd worked. And there she'd lived for over two months, searching for his whereabouts all the while.*

393
00:44:16,000 --> 00:44:19,000
Fuminori: "Don't you have to go to school?"

394
00:44:19,000 --> 00:44:24,000
Saya: "No, Dad taught me everything I need to know. I'm really smart."

395
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:40,000
*She was a strange girl. On the one hand, she looked and talked like an innocent child.  On the other, she was remarkably self-reliant, and at times exhibited a sharp intelligence and deep knowledge that many may have found unsettling.*

396
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:49,000
*I didn't care. Saya was the only other human in a world gone mad. Her existence meant far more to me than the standards of society.*

397
00:44:49,000 --> 00:44:52,000
Fuminori: "Aren't you worried you might get caught?"

398
00:44:52,000 --> 00:45:00,000
Saya: "Nope! I don't have to worry about food here, and it's a lot more fun than staying in Dad's house by myself."

399
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:20,000
Saya: "I looked through the patient lists and found the ones who have mental problems," Saya continued, grinning mischievously. "Sometimes I sneak into their rooms late at night and scare them. Even if they raise a fuss, no one believes what mental patients say. They just brush it off as a bad dream."

400
00:45:20,000 --> 00:45:32,000
*Her confession reminded me that the hospital was famous for its ghost stories. Who could have imagined that there was actually a real girl impishly roaming these hallways?*

401
00:45:32,000 --> 00:45:36,000
Fuminori: "So that's why you came to my room the first time?"

402
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:38,000
Saya: "Yeah, sorry. Are you mad?"

403
00:45:38,000 --> 00:45:47,000
*While her pranks were hardly praiseworthy, I couldn't bring myself to scold her for the very thing that had brought us together.*

404
00:45:47,000 --> 00:45:52,000
Fuminori: "You shouldn't do it anymore. Will you come talk to me instead?"

405
00:45:52,000 --> 00:45:55,000
Saya: "Yeah! That's more fun for me, too!"

406
00:45:55,000 --> 00:45:59,000
*With extreme care, I was able to conceal my sensory disorder.*

407
00:45:59,000 --> 00:46:10,000
*It was glaringly obvious that the doctors had no way to cure me, and the fact that I had undergone a still-experimental procedure made me even more cautious.*

408
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:26,000
*As a medical student, it was easy for me to imagine how the doctors would react if they discovered that I was exhibiting such unusual side effects. I was not about to become a guinea pig, a mere specimen to be examined with clinical detachment.*

409
00:46:26,000 --> 00:46:36,000
*And so I hid my discomfort and loathing behind a mask of normalcy, convincing the doctors that any signs of stress were merely a result of hospitalization.*

410
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:43,000
*Saya was my support. Looking forward to her nightly visits gave me the strength to endure my daily torture.*

411
00:46:43,000 --> 00:46:53,000
*Hope can make an enormous difference in a patient's progress. With the aid of my secret nurse, I recovered at a pace that left the doctors stunned.*

412
00:46:53,000 --> 00:47:01,000
*On the last night before my release, I summoned my courage and asked her, "Are you going to stay here forever?"*

413
00:47:01,000 --> 00:47:10,000
Saya: "Yeah. I couldn't learn anything about my dad, but it's not like I have anywhere else to go. I guess I'll stay as long as I can hide."

414
00:47:10,000 --> 00:47:13,000
*In other words, she had no reason to stay.*

415
00:47:13,000 --> 00:47:19,000
Fuminori: "Why not stay with me?" I asked timidly. The question took all the courage I had.

416
00:47:19,000 --> 00:47:20,000
Saya: "Huh?"

417
00:47:20,000 --> 00:47:28,000
Fuminori: "My family's gone, so I have plenty of room! You won't need to hide, and it's not a bad place to live!"

418
00:47:28,000 --> 00:47:30,000
Saya: "You want me to live with you?"

419
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
*I was too afraid to ask her what she thought of that, so I hastily offered a deal.*

420
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:42,000
Fuminori: "In exchange, I'll help you look for your father! I'll find him no matter what!"

421
00:47:42,000 --> 00:47:47,000
Saya: "I think that's gonna be hard," Saya said, looking a little embarassed.

422
00:47:47,000 --> 00:47:52,000
Saya:  can't get the police involved. You'll have to be as discrete as possible."

423
00:47:52,000 --> 00:47:55,000
Fuminori: "I'll do whatever it takes! I..."

424
00:47:55,000 --> 00:47:59,000
*Unable to control myself, I finally spoke the truth.*

425
00:47:59,000 --> 00:48:02,000
Fuminori: "I can't be apart from you."

426
00:48:02,000 --> 00:48:09,000
*At first she looked bewildered, but after a few moments of silence, she said, "Give me a little time."*

427
00:48:09,000 --> 00:48:12,000
*That night, she left my room earlier than usual.*

428
00:48:12,000 --> 00:48:19,000
*On the day of my release, I managed to smile as I accepted the hideous, foul-smelling celebratory bouquet.*

429
00:48:19,000 --> 00:48:32,000
*The flesh-beasts calling themselves Koji, Omi, and Yoh came to pick me up. Though they had come to see me many times during my stay, it never got easier to see my friends changed so horribly.*

430
00:48:32,000 --> 00:48:38,000
*My sudden tears of despair drew suspicion, but I managed to explain them away as tears of joy.*

431
00:48:38,000 --> 00:48:51,000
*While we walked to Koji's car, I looked desperately for Saya amid the grotesque scenery. Even as we drove away, I kept watching the hospital fade into the distance, praying for a last glimmer of hope.*

432
00:48:51,000 --> 00:48:53,000
*But Saya never appeared.*

433
00:48:53,000 --> 00:49:06,000
*After Koji and the others dropped me off, I paused a while to regard my surroundings. I had lived my entire life on this block, in this house. There was no other place that I could call home.*

434
00:49:06,000 --> 00:49:08,000
*But nothing was as I remembered.*

435
00:49:08,000 --> 00:49:20,000
*As I walked up the path to the front door and took in the yard where I had spent my childhood, I could feel those memories being defiled by the twisted, festering shapes around me.*

436
00:49:20,000 --> 00:49:29,000
*Inside the house, I found nothing familiar, nothing to offer me comfort and warmth. What I had once called home was now a whole other world.*

437
00:49:29,000 --> 00:49:38,000
Fuminori: "I have no home," I whispered with a smile of self-pity. There was one last stop to make. One last nail to hammer into my coffin.

438
00:49:38,000 --> 00:49:49,000
*I stepped into the room that had cradled me from childhood. The walls were papered with human entrails, the bed a tangled mass of wormflesh. But none of that mattered.*

439
00:49:49,000 --> 00:49:53,000
*There, curled up on the bed like an abandoned cat, was Saya.*

440
00:49:53,000 --> 00:50:00,000
*As I stood there in shock, she looked up at me and in a tiny, weak voice said, "Can I really stay?"*

441
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
*I responded by sweeping her into my arms, embracing her tightly so that she would not escape.*

442
00:50:06,000 --> 00:50:07,000
*Saya did not resist.*

443
00:50:07,000 --> 00:50:13,000
*When she arrives at the Sakisaka house, Omi first takes a deep breath to calm herself.*

444
00:50:13,000 --> 00:50:19,000
*Her anger does not vanish entirely, of course, but at least now she can hear herself think.*

445
00:50:19,000 --> 00:50:27,000
*While waiting for a response from the intercom, she looks over the patch of yard that she can see from outside the gate.*

446
00:50:27,000 --> 00:50:34,000
*Even Omi isn't normally one to complain about other people's housekeeping, but this is going too far.*

447
00:50:34,000 --> 00:50:44,000
*The grass is growing wild, and there are piles of dead leaves scattered everywhere. It doesn't just look untended. It looks like an uninhabited ruin.*

448
00:50:44,000 --> 00:50:53,000
*It's still light out, but every window has its storm shutters tightly sealed. Omi guesses that they've been closed since morning.*

449
00:50:53,000 --> 00:51:00,000
*What kind of life is Fuminori leading? Even if he's living alone, he can't neglect his housework forever.*

450
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:08,000
*And is it just her imagination, or does something stink like rotten meat? It couldn't be coming from the yard, could it?*

451
00:51:08,000 --> 00:51:22,000
*There's still no response, so she presses the buzzer a second time, and a third, and a fourth. Finally, after this has gone on for over ten minutes, Omi loses her patience and opens the cover of the intercom.*

452
00:51:22,000 --> 00:51:25,000
*As she expected, the power has been disconnected.*

453
00:51:25,000 --> 00:51:39,000
*Perhaps Fuminori has a good reason for shutting out the world, but Omi can only see it as a lack of respect for others. Her anger rekindled, she pushes the gate open and stomps through the yard to the front door.*

454
00:51:39,000 --> 00:51:52,000
*Given the state of his intercom, she doubts that Fuminori will respond to a knock, so Omi decides to simply open the door and go in shouting. And if the door is locked, she'll just have to...*

455
00:51:52,000 --> 00:52:01,000
*Surprisingly, the doorknob turns easily in her hand, and the enraged Omi finds herself throwing the door open wider than she intended.*

456
00:52:01,000 --> 00:52:05,000
*Her nostrils are instantly assaulted by a choking stench.*

457
00:52:05,000 --> 00:52:07,000
Oumi: "((What is that smell!?))

458
00:52:07,000 --> 00:52:15,000
*As Omi stands petrified on the threshold, the cowbell hanging on the inside of the door chimes loudly. A moment later...*

459
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:16,000
Saya: "WeLCoMe HOMe!"

460
00:52:16,000 --> 00:52:26,000
*Omi can't believe her ears. The voice she just heard could not have been human, yet its intonations were too complex for any animal she can imagine.*

461
00:52:26,000 --> 00:52:32,000
Oumi: "Is someone there?" she calls out to the end of the hallway from which the voice came.

462
00:52:32,000 --> 00:52:40,000
*There is no response. Instead, she hears the sound of something soft and wet flopping its way deeper into the house.*

463
00:52:40,000 --> 00:52:41,000
Oumi: "......"

464
00:52:41,000 --> 00:52:52,000
*Finding it difficult to place a meaningful image to the voice she just heard, Omi stares blankly at the empty vestibule. There's nothing there somewhere, wearing them.*

465
00:52:52,000 --> 00:52:56,000
*The house should be empty. But then what was that voice just now?*

466
00:52:56,000 --> 00:53:06,000
*Her anger has vanished as if it were never there. Nevertheless, Omi sets foot into the hallway, leaving the door open so that the cowbell won't ring.*

467
00:53:06,000 --> 00:53:17,000
*The floor creaks, setting her nerves on edge. Omi herself isn't sure why she's acting like a burglar, but something tells her to make as little noise as possible.*

468
00:53:17,000 --> 00:53:32,000
*The potency of the stink inside the house makes the whiff she caught outside pale in comparison. It's sickening, like rotten fish guts. Has food been left to spoil in the kitchen? She hears a bubbling sound up ahead.*

469
00:53:32,000 --> 00:53:45,000
*Stepping gingerly on the creaking floorboards, Omi makes her way to the end of the hallway. She finds rooms to both sides of her -- one lit, the other dark -- and chooses to look into the lit room.*

470
00:53:45,000 --> 00:53:52,000
*It's the kitchen, lit by what must be the only window in the house not covered by a storm shutter.*

471
00:53:52,000 --> 00:54:10,000
*The sound she heard was the pot boiling on the stove, and on the chopping board next to it lie a butcher's knife and some half-diced carrots. A perfectly normal household scene, with the light of the setting sun making everything the color of decomposing fruit.*

472
00:54:10,000 --> 00:54:14,000
*Something is wrong. Who was cooking here? And where did they go?*

473
00:54:14,000 --> 00:54:27,000
Oumi: "Is anyone here?" Omi calls, regretting it immediately as she realizes that her voice is shaking. As her words echo vainly through the silent house, she begins to feel foolish and defenseless.

474
00:54:27,000 --> 00:54:31,000
*Suddenly she feels something cold seeping through her pantyhose.*

475
00:54:31,000 --> 00:54:48,000
*She timidly reaches down to touch her feet. Her fingertips come away covered with a viscous, olive green slime, like the filthy water from a tank long clogged with algae and dead fish. The whole floor is covered with it. It must be the source of the stench.*

476
00:54:48,000 --> 00:54:53,000
*Omi now wishes that she had worn her shoes inside, manners be damned.*

477
00:54:53,000 --> 00:55:05,000
*When she looks back ruefully the way she came, she realizes that her current position is not visible from the entrance. This kitchen must be where that strange voice came from.*

478
00:55:05,000 --> 00:55:12,000
*The next room is probably the den. As she expected from the closed storm shutters, it's pitch black inside.*

479
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:22,000
*Omi wants nothing more than to flee this house, but that would mean turning her back to the darkness. And that, she simply cannot bring herself to do.*

480
00:55:22,000 --> 00:55:26,000
*Moved by some irrational compulsion, Omi sets foot into the den.*

481
00:55:26,000 --> 00:55:31,000
*It is too dark to see anything, and the stink is far worse than before.*

482
00:55:31,000 --> 00:55:41,000
*She slides her hand along the wall, feeling for the light switch. Finding it much sooner than she expected, she flips it on like it's her last hope.*

483
00:55:41,000 --> 00:55:43,000
*Colors. Colors. So many colors.*

484
00:55:43,000 --> 00:56:02,000
*The purple of entrails, the brown of rotten meat, the crimson of fresh blood, the yellow of fat -- these colors, and more that cannot be described, cover every inch of the room in maddening array. The colors say all that needs to be said about the painter's hatred, malice, and insanity.*

485
00:56:02,000 --> 00:56:13,000
Oumi: "Omi's legs give out from the shock, sending her to the floor. Slime immediately soaks through her jeans, its cold tendrils creeping up her legs, crotch, and...

486
00:56:13,000 --> 00:56:14,000
*Her neck.*

487
00:56:14,000 --> 00:56:19,000
*Her hand flies to her neck, where it is greeted by another drop of chilly slime.*

488
00:56:19,000 --> 00:56:22,000
*Above her. Something is dripping down on her head.*

489
00:56:22,000 --> 00:56:26,000
*Making perhaps the worst decision of her life, Omi looks up.*

490
00:56:26,000 --> 00:56:33,000
*The predator clinging to the ceiling, poised to leap upon its prey -- she sees it in every detail.*

491
00:56:33,000 --> 00:56:41,000
*Her mouth and nose are sealed before she can scream, and her belly is torn open as something enters to feast on her innards.*

492
00:56:41,000 --> 00:56:45,000
*But by the time she feels any of this, Omi has already gone mad.*

493
00:56:45,000 --> 00:56:53,000
*I bit the bullet and tried to take the train, but the rush hour crowds were so bad that I had to get off halfway and walk.*

494
00:56:53,000 --> 00:56:57,000
*I'm running pretty late. Is Saya worried? I hope she's not mad.*

495
00:56:57,000 --> 00:57:02,000
*When I enter the yard, I realize that the front door has been left wide open.*

496
00:57:02,000 --> 00:57:13,000
*Light from the living room is seeping out into the hallway, and I hear what sounds like someone smacking their lips. There's also a tantalizing fragrance in the air.*

497
00:57:13,000 --> 00:57:19,000
*Is it Saya? I consider calling out to her, but decide to enter in silence instead.*

498
00:57:19,000 --> 00:57:27,000
*Something smells strange, though not unpleasant. The aroma is quite soothing, in fact. It reminds me of Saya's hair.*

499
00:57:27,000 --> 00:57:31,000
*At first, I am surprised by what I see in the living room.*

500
00:57:31,000 --> 00:57:44,000
*The floor is covered with what looks to be some kind of grass -- probably the source of the herblike smell -- and there are fruit or vegetable-like balls of varying size scattered everywhere.*

501
00:57:44,000 --> 00:57:45,000
Fuminori: "Saya?"

502
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:46,000
Saya: "Ah!"

503
00:57:46,000 --> 00:57:54,000
*Saya turns around, her eyes wide with surprise. She then looks away sheepishly, like a child caught at some prank.*

504
00:57:54,000 --> 00:57:56,000
Fuminori: "What are you eating?"

505
00:57:56,000 --> 00:58:03,000
Saya: "This is, um, well," she stammers, so flustered that I suddenly feel bad for sneaking up on her.

506
00:58:03,000 --> 00:58:10,000
*Remembering that she has never eaten in front of me before, I realize that she must be quite embarassed.*

507
00:58:10,000 --> 00:58:12,000
Fuminori: "Can I have one?"

508
00:58:12,000 --> 00:58:19,000
*I scoop up the closest fruit-thing and pop it into my mouth, ignoring Saya's attempt to wave me off.*

509
00:58:19,000 --> 00:58:34,000
*It has a strange texture, soft and pliable, like a peach or a pear. When I bite into it with my back teeth, a succulent juice fills my mouth, combined with a sharp, strong fragrance. It's unlike anything I've ever tasted.*

510
00:58:34,000 --> 00:58:37,000
Fuminori: "How did you make this? What did you use?"

511
00:58:37,000 --> 00:58:45,000
Saya: "It wasn't hard... I just took it apart and melted it a little to make it easier to eat. It's practically raw."

512
00:58:45,000 --> 00:58:46,000
Fuminori: "Oh?"

513
00:58:46,000 --> 00:58:57,000
*I pick up a different lump, this one consisting of fruity flesh around a hard core. Tearing a chunk off in my mouth, I find that it has a similar taste to the last one.*

514
00:58:57,000 --> 00:59:00,000
Saya: "Hey, are you okay? That's a..."

515
00:59:00,000 --> 00:59:04,000
Fuminori: "Yeah, even I can eat this. In fact, it's good!"

516
00:59:04,000 --> 00:59:05,000
Saya: "Really?"

517
00:59:05,000 --> 00:59:09,000
*At first Saya looks dumbstruck, but then she bursts out laughing.*

518
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:14,000
Saya: "So this is what you like! Now I feel stupid for going to all that trouble."

519
00:59:14,000 --> 00:59:17,000
Fuminori: "Is this what you always eat, Saya?"

520
00:59:17,000 --> 00:59:24,000
Saya: "Yeah, though it's been a while since I've had one so big. I usually catch them in the nearby park."

521
00:59:24,000 --> 00:59:38,000
*There's an impressive nature preserve not too far from here. I've never heard about fruits like these growing there, but -- well, of course. They only look like fruits to me. They're really something else.*

522
00:59:38,000 --> 00:59:41,000
Saya: "Sorry, I already ate the best parts."

523
00:59:41,000 --> 00:59:46,000
Fuminori: "That's okay. There's always next time, and now we can eat together."

524
00:59:46,000 --> 00:59:47,000
Saya: "Yeah!"

525
00:59:47,000 --> 00:59:57,000
*Saya seems really happy. I'm happy too, of course. Eating with someone is much more fun than eating alone, and it makes the food taste better too.*

526
00:59:57,000 --> 01:00:04,000
Saya: "There's still plenty left. It'll keep chilled for two or three days, though it won't taste as good."

527
01:00:04,000 --> 01:00:07,000
Fuminori: "Then we'd better start putting it away."

528
01:00:07,000 --> 01:00:20,000
*Sealing the small fruits in tupperware and the large ones in pots and bowls, Saya and I store the remaining food in the refrigerator. Thinking of tomorrow's dinner fills me with anticipation.*

529
01:00:20,000 --> 01:00:25,000
*I feel that, little by little, I'm starting to regain the joy of living.*

530
01:00:25,000 --> 01:00:28,000
*Saya will guide me. With her, I can live on.*

531
01:00:28,000 --> 01:00:29,000
*True Scary Stories*

532
01:00:29,000 --> 01:00:30,000
*Hospital Edition*

533
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:33,000
Chapter 4: The Monster in the University Hospital

534
01:00:33,000 --> 01:00:41,000
*A research student relates his shocking experiences at Tokyo's most prestigious hospital! Will you believe him or not!?*

535
01:00:41,000 --> 01:00:46,000
*Strange things started happening at the hospital around the end of last spring.*

536
01:00:46,000 --> 01:01:00,000
*It began with patients waking up in the middle of the night, screaming. They all spoke of terrifying nightmares, and many of them had to be sedated. Some patients even transferred to other hospitals because of it.*

537
01:01:00,000 --> 01:01:10,000
*The weird thing was that they'd all had exactly the same dream -- a dream about some horribly disgusting monster staring down at them from their bedside.*

538
01:01:10,000 --> 01:01:14,000
*But the really strange stuff started happening after that.*

539
01:01:14,000 --> 01:01:20,000
*There used to be a lot of stray cats around campus, looking for scraps from the students.*

540
01:01:20,000 --> 01:01:29,000
*One day, the cats suddenly disappeared, and it wasn't that they'd stopped coming. It was more like they'd vanished from the area entirely.*

541
01:01:29,000 --> 01:01:38,000
*And then people stopped walking their dogs around. According to rumors, the dogs were refusing to go anywhere near the school.*

542
01:01:38,000 --> 01:01:42,000
*Eventually, things started going missing in the hospital.*

543
01:01:42,000 --> 01:01:44,000
*Organs, to be precise.*

544
01:01:44,000 --> 01:02:01,000
*Transplant organs kept disappearing from storage. Some people came close to losing their jobs over it. And it wasn't just two or three times that it happened. They tried to keep it from the research students, but we heard that it was a lot worse than that.*

545
01:02:01,000 --> 01:02:06,000
*People started saying that there was something living in the hospital.*

546
01:02:06,000 --> 01:02:22,000
*The janitors would find strange messes that could only have been made in the middle of the night -- traces of something that had crawled down the hallway, or weird stains that seemed to be caused by something dripping through the ceiling.*

547
01:02:22,000 --> 01:02:29,000
*The late-shift nurses talked about hearing strange noises on the same nights that patients woke screaming.*

548
01:02:29,000 --> 01:02:34,000
*There's one last story, one you can never mention inside the hospital.*

549
01:02:34,000 --> 01:02:37,000
*One day, the obstetrics department went crazy.*

550
01:02:37,000 --> 01:02:41,000
*They said that a newborn had disappeared in the night.*

551
01:02:41,000 --> 01:02:53,000
*If that were true, the police would've come and it would've been all over the news, but they say the big shots managed to make it all go away. It's just a rumor, of course.*

552
01:02:53,000 --> 01:02:58,000
*These strange incidents suddenly stopped towards the end of summer.*

553
01:02:58,000 --> 01:03:05,000
*Now there are almost no patients complaining of nightmares, and the cats have started coming back to campus.*

554
01:03:05,000 --> 01:03:12,000
*But still, what happened in the hospital that summer? Even now, just thinking about it gives me the creeps.*

555
01:03:12,000 --> 01:03:13,000
*...........*

556
01:03:13,000 --> 01:03:14,000
Koji: "Nothing."

557
01:03:14,000 --> 01:03:15,000
Yoh: "......"

558
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:21,000
*This is the third day in a row that they haven't been able to get in touch with Omi.*

559
01:03:21,000 --> 01:03:31,000
*There's no sign that she returned to her apartment, and even her family doesn't know anything. Her parents have already filed a missing persons report.*

560
01:03:31,000 --> 01:03:37,000
Koji: "Well, you know her. She'll probably just pop up somewhere like nothing happened."

561
01:03:37,000 --> 01:03:49,000
Yoh: "I hope so," Yoh replies with a gloomy expression. She's worried about Omi, of course, but the incident with Fuminori three days ago must still be weighing on her mind as well.

562
01:03:49,000 --> 01:04:01,000
*Yoh hasn't seen Fuminori since then, and Fuminori hasn't made any effort to approach her or Koji. Four people used to meet in this cafeteria between classes, but now there are only two.*

563
01:04:01,000 --> 01:04:06,000
Yoh: "Hey, Koji, let's keep thinking. Isn't there somewhere Omi might have gone?"

564
01:04:06,000 --> 01:04:10,000
Koji: "No," Koji answers evasively. "I already checked everywhere."

565
01:04:10,000 --> 01:04:19,000
*It's a lie, of course. Koji knows where Omi planned to go that evening, but he doesn't want to bring Fuminori up in front of Yoh.*

566
01:04:19,000 --> 01:04:25,000
*Their awkward silence is mercifully broken by the bell signaling the start of the next period.*

567
01:04:25,000 --> 01:04:27,000
Koji: "Well, I've gotta go."

568
01:04:27,000 --> 01:04:28,000
Yoh: "......Yeah."

569
01:04:28,000 --> 01:04:36,000
*If Koji isn't mistaken, Yoh is supposed to have class next period too, but she just sits there, staring off into space.*

570
01:04:36,000 --> 01:04:41,000
*Unable to come up with anything to say, he leaves the cafeteria reluctantly.*

571
01:04:41,000 --> 01:04:48,000
*Both Omi's disappearance and Yoh's depression worry Koji, and both problems lead back to the exact same place.*

572
01:04:48,000 --> 01:04:51,000
Koji: "((What the hell is Fuminori doing?))

573
01:04:51,000 --> 01:05:03,000
*When Omi went missing, the first thing he did was question Fuminori. After all, the last time he'd seen her was just before she stormed off to give Fuminori a piece of her mind.*

574
01:05:03,000 --> 01:05:18,000
*Fuminori responded with unequivocal denial, and acted like he hadn't the slightest idea why Omi would have gone to see him. Perhaps that was only natural, as he was unaware that Omi and Koji had witnessed him reduce Yoh to tears.*

575
01:05:18,000 --> 01:05:29,000
*Did Omi even make it to Fuminori's house? She had been riding a wave of emotion when she'd left, and might have calmed down and changed her mind halfway there.*

576
01:05:29,000 --> 01:05:32,000
*Or perhaps she ran into trouble on the way?*

577
01:05:32,000 --> 01:05:49,000
Koji concluded -- or, more accurately, convinced himself -- that one of these possibilities was the truth, subconsciously denying the one remaining possibility: that Fuminori was lying -- that he had met Omi, and was involved with her disappearance.

578
01:05:49,000 --> 01:06:01,000
*When questioned by the police, Koji told the truth about Omi's destination only up to the train station, maintaining that he had no idea where she'd planned to go after that.*

579
01:06:01,000 --> 01:06:15,000
*He wanted to cooperate with the search, of course, but Omi couldn't have made it to Fuminori's house. Fuminori said so himself, didn't he? In that case, he'd told the police everything they needed to know.*

580
01:06:15,000 --> 01:06:22,000
*Not wanting to get the still-fragile Fuminori involved, he forced himself to accept this flimsy logic.*

581
01:06:22,000 --> 01:06:30,000
*But the conflict has built up inside of him without his notice, leaving unanswered suspicion to fester in his mind.*

582
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:42,000
*Koji is deep in thought, paying no attention to his surroundings, but perhaps that is what allows him to catch sight of his friend's back through the crowd of milling students.*

583
01:06:42,000 --> 01:06:43,000
Koji: "((Fuminori?))

584
01:06:43,000 --> 01:06:51,000
*At first, Koji assumes that he's headed to the lecture hall, but it soon appears that he is instead going home.*

585
01:06:51,000 --> 01:06:55,000
*Strange. Medical students have required courses in the afternoon.*

586
01:06:55,000 --> 01:07:00,000
*Though he is initially surprised, Koji's hesitation lasts for only a second.*

587
01:07:00,000 --> 01:07:06,000
*He follows his friend, taking care to stay far enough behind that he won't be noticed.*

588
01:07:06,000 --> 01:07:13,000
*Fuminori wasn't going home, as became obvious when he boarded a train heading in the opposite direction.*

589
01:07:13,000 --> 01:07:23,000
*Koji's next guess was that he was going to see his doctor at the T University Hospital, but Fuminori rode straight through the closest station.*

590
01:07:23,000 --> 01:07:25,000
Koji: "((Where is he going?))

591
01:07:25,000 --> 01:07:34,000
*At first, Koji felt ashamed for tailing his friend like this, but his conscience fell silent as Fuminori's actions grew more mysterious.*

592
01:07:34,000 --> 01:07:45,000
*The stranger it gets, the closer Koji feels to discovering the truth behind Fuminori's sudden transformation. Any knowledge would be welcome, no matter how slight.*

593
01:07:45,000 --> 01:07:59,000
*Even Koji is beginning to think that there must be more behind Fuminori's change than the accident alone. He wants a more satisfying answer, one that will help him decide whether Fuminori can still be trusted.*

594
01:07:59,000 --> 01:08:10,000
*Fuminori gets off at a small station in a nondescript suburb of Tokyo. Koji follows, trying not to lose sight of him amid the other disembarking passengers.*

595
01:08:10,000 --> 01:08:21,000
*The area is quite desolate, with only a small bookstore, a convenience store, and a market in front of the train station. It is easy for Koji to keep Fuminori in view.*

596
01:08:21,000 --> 01:08:36,000
*This neighboorhood was carved out of the Fuji foothills, and here and there remain steep inclines and wooded areas that escaped assimilation. Koji is amazed that such a quiet place exists less than an hour out of central Tokyo.*

597
01:08:36,000 --> 01:08:45,000
*Fuminori seems to know these streets. He moves quickly and purposefully through the suburban community, his eyes fixed straight ahead.*

598
01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:58,000
*Before long, Fuminori reaches a house. Without ringing the bell or even knocking, he opens the door and vanishes inside, leaving Koji to wonder how Fuminori can treat the house as his own.*

599
01:08:58,000 --> 01:09:05,000
*After waiting to see if Fuminori comes back out, Koji approaches the gate and checks the nameplate.*

600
01:09:05,000 --> 01:09:06,000
*Ogai, it reads.*

601
01:09:06,000 --> 01:09:11,000
*Koji has never heard of anyone by that name among Fuminori's acquaintances.*

602
01:09:11,000 --> 01:09:25,000
*Next, his attention is drawn to the thick wad of leaflets sticking out of the mail slot. This, coupled with the general dilapidated feel of the place, suggests that it has been abandonded for some time.*

603
01:09:25,000 --> 01:09:39,000
*A small playground about two blocks away provides an adequate vantage point from which to watch the front of the Ogai home. Fortunately, it does not appear to be the sort of house that has a rear exit.*

604
01:09:39,000 --> 01:09:43,000
*Koji settles down on a bench to begin his stakeout.*

605
01:09:43,000 --> 01:09:46,000
*((I should've brought more smokes.))*

606
01:09:46,000 --> 01:09:56,000
*One hour passes, and then another, but there remains no sign of movement around the Ogai residence. Soon twilight settles upon the neighborhood.*

607
01:09:56,000 --> 01:10:12,000
*After Koji's one pack of cigarettes runs out, the stakeout becomes a battle against mounting impatience. He kills time by redialing Omi on his cell and sending her short text messages, but his efforts are futile, as he knew they would be.*

608
01:10:12,000 --> 01:10:24,000
*When the sky begins to turn deep blue and the streetlights come on, Fuminori finally emerges from the house and heads back towards the station with the same hurried stride.*

609
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:32,000
*After some brief consideration, Koji decides that right now, investigating the house is more important than tailing Fuminori.*

610
01:10:32,000 --> 01:10:43,000
*He rings the doorbell just to make sure. After receiving the expected silence in response, he checks to make sure no one is watching and turns the doorknob.*

611
01:10:43,000 --> 01:10:45,000
*The door is not locked.*

612
01:10:45,000 --> 01:10:56,000
*The moment he enters the house, stale air thick with mold and dust fills Koji's nostrils. It is the unmistakable smell of a house that has long lain untouched.*

613
01:10:56,000 --> 01:11:04,000
*There is also a faint hint of something else in the air, something reminiscent of damp sewers and fetid cisterns.*

614
01:11:04,000 --> 01:11:09,000
*Flipping the light switch does nothing. The power must be cut off.*

615
01:11:09,000 --> 01:11:28,000
*Koji uses his cigarette lighter to illuminate the immediate area. In the thick dust covering the floor, he sees several brand-new trails of footprints that could only have been made by shoes -- Fuminori's. Koji decides to follow suit and dispense with courtesy. He enters with his shoes on.*

616
01:11:28,000 --> 01:11:34,000
*The lighter's flickering flame pushes back the deathly silence and gloom of the house.*

617
01:11:34,000 --> 01:11:43,000
*Koji is surprised to see evidence of life remaining -- everything from furniture to tableware and appliances. Nothing seems to be missing.*

618
01:11:43,000 --> 01:11:57,000
*The thickness of the dust suggests that the house has been empty for several months, which means that the owner must have left with little more than the clothes on his back. Could he have gone on a long vacation?*

619
01:11:57,000 --> 01:12:00,000
*The calendar in the den is still turned to April.*

620
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:16,000
*Empty and silent, yet still exhibiting signs of the life that was once lived there, the house reminds Koji of a passenger ship entombed at the bottom of the sea. In the graveyard-like quiet, a sinister thought suddenly enters his mind.*

621
01:12:16,000 --> 01:12:26,000
*No one is living here, but that does not have to mean that the owner left. Maybe he was murdered, and his rotting corpse is right under Koji's feet.*

622
01:12:26,000 --> 01:12:33,000
*He finds himself wanting a stronger light. A flashlight in his hand would make him feel much better.*

623
01:12:33,000 --> 01:12:48,000
*Koji follows Fuminori's footsteps to the second floor, where he begins to catch the scent of paper in the stale air. It is the smell of old books, instantly recognizable to anyone who has worked in an antique bookstore or library.*

624
01:12:48,000 --> 01:13:09,000
*The first room on the second floor turns out to be a study, its towering shelves packed with such a vast number of books that Koji fears for the stability of the floor. As a medical student himself, he is able to discern at a glance that this study belongs to a medical professional, and a high-level one at that.*

625
01:13:09,000 --> 01:13:22,000
*Judging by the content of the books, a smorgasbord of technical volumes far beyond a simple student's understanding, the owner's interests lie more with medical research than with clinical practice.*

626
01:13:22,000 --> 01:13:34,000
*Fuminori must have spent most of his time here. The scattered dust suggests that he was searching for something, and the contents of the desk drawers are in obvious disarray.*

627
01:13:34,000 --> 01:13:49,000
*A small pile of books stacked on the side table catches his eye. Being next to the desk, they must have been the most frequently read. Their nature could shed some light on the character of the person who worked here.*

628
01:13:49,000 --> 01:14:01,000
*Koji frowns as he examines the three books. These aren't scientific texts like the rest, but old, leather-bound Western tomes like the sort you would find in a rare book store.*

629
01:14:01,000 --> 01:14:11,000
*The titles are meaningless to him. Traite des Chiffres appears to concern semiotics, but Ars Magna et Ultima is some kind of treatise on... divination?*

630
01:14:11,000 --> 01:14:27,000
*And then there's the Voynich Manuscript, which looks like some sort of picture book.<se id="1" src="pageturn" mode="normal" loop="off"> When he pages through it, he finds the text utterly incomprehensible. Maybe it's some kind of cipher.*

631
01:14:27,000 --> 01:14:36,000
*Whatever they are, they clearly have nothing to do with medicine, refuting Koji's earlier guess that this "Ogai" was a doctor.*

632
01:14:36,000 --> 01:14:43,000
*Looking down, Koji suddenly notices the glint of something black and metallic underneath the chair.*

633
01:14:43,000 --> 01:14:50,000
*A pocket-sized flashlight, quite out of place among all these dusty books. Fuminori must have brought it in.*

634
01:14:50,000 --> 01:14:59,000
*With relief, Koji exchanges his lighter for the flashlight. Its tiny body emits a powerful white beam that casts away the darkness.*

635
01:14:59,000 --> 01:15:04,000
*His courage restored, he decides to explore the rest of the house.*

636
01:15:04,000 --> 01:15:05,000
Koji: "......Hm?"

637
01:15:05,000 --> 01:15:11,000
*Koji notices something strange, something that was not visible in the lighter's weak flame.*

638
01:15:11,000 --> 01:15:12,000
*The slime.*

639
01:15:12,000 --> 01:15:23,000
*Dark, oily stains are everywhere. The stains are especially thick around the doorknobs and stair banisters, like someone grasped them with hands wrapped in greasy cloth.*

640
01:15:23,000 --> 01:15:32,000
*Looking closer, he sees places where slime was splashed low on the walls, almost as if a wet mop was run violently across the floor.*

641
01:15:32,000 --> 01:15:33,000
Koji: "......"

642
01:15:33,000 --> 01:15:43,000
*Could Ogai have made these marks? If so, how? Koji begins to feel sick as he imagines a man shambling through the house with slime dripping from his body.*

643
01:15:43,000 --> 01:15:48,000
*Finding the bedroom next to the study, Koji checks the closet on a hunch.*

644
01:15:48,000 --> 01:15:55,000
*He discovers two empty suitcases -- not what one would leave behind when going on a long vacation.*

645
01:15:55,000 --> 01:16:01,000
*A sudden chill runs through him. Whoever was living here is still somewhere inside the house.*

646
01:16:01,000 --> 01:16:07,000
*Suppressing the urge to flee, Koji goes back downstairs to check the first floor.*

647
01:16:07,000 --> 01:16:22,000
*If he finds a corpse, he'll have to call the police right away. He might get away with trespassing if he reports it first, but if they find the body later, it'll be awfully hard to explain his fingerprints all over the house.*

648
01:16:22,000 --> 01:16:33,000
*The flashlight reveals the den to be covered in even more slime than the rest of the house. The sofa looks as though it was dredged from the bottom of a swamp.*

649
01:16:33,000 --> 01:16:42,000
*In the kitchen, Koji takes one look at the sink and decides not to get any closer. He doesn't want any more fuel for his imagination.*

650
01:16:42,000 --> 01:16:45,000
*He reaches the door to the bathroom.*

651
01:16:45,000 --> 01:16:53,000
*A common scene from TV dramas flashes through his head -- a body with slit wrists floating in a bathtub full of water.*

652
01:16:53,000 --> 01:16:59,000
*And wasn't there a movie where a hitman disposes of his victim in a bathtub filled with lye?*

653
01:16:59,000 --> 01:17:10,000
*Koji braces himself for the worst and opens the door slowly, then shines his light into the ceramic bathtub that appears from the darkness like a white ghost.*

654
01:17:10,000 --> 01:17:14,000
*Bones. So many bones. Bones black with dry flesh and blood.*

655
01:17:14,000 --> 01:17:26,000
*Koji puts one hand against the wall to steady himself as his legs threaten to buckle. Something is wrong, he realizes as he tries desperately to get his thoughts in order.*

656
01:17:26,000 --> 01:17:30,000
*The bones are too small, and there are far too many of them.*

657
01:17:30,000 --> 01:17:31,000
*They aren't human.*

658
01:17:31,000 --> 01:17:38,000
*After taking several deep breaths to calm himself, Koji enters the bathroom and examines the tub.*

659
01:17:38,000 --> 01:17:46,000
*The bones are piled atop each other like fallen leaves. They appear to be from small animals, perhaps cats or dogs.*

660
01:17:46,000 --> 01:17:53,000
*Even so, the quantity is mind-boggling. How many bodies would it take to produce this many bones?*

661
01:17:53,000 --> 01:18:07,000
*The bones have all been separated from one another, so it doesn't look like bodies were just thrown into the tub and left to rot. Each bone is covered with deep grooves -- marks left by teeth biting through flesh.*

662
01:18:07,000 --> 01:18:13,000
*Koji's sanity won't let him consider the possibility that a human could have done this.*

663
01:18:13,000 --> 01:18:35,000
*The owner of this house must have kept some sort of carnivorous animal as a pet, giving it the bones of small animals to eat and disposing of the remains in the bathtub. But why not dispose of the leftovers properly? They could have just been thrown out with the garbage. Or was there something keeping him from leaving the house?*

664
01:18:35,000 --> 01:18:41,000
*The relief Koji felt when he realized that the bones weren't human is once again under attack.*

665
01:18:41,000 --> 01:18:45,000
*In the first place, what the hell was Fuminori doing here?*

666
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:46,000
Koji: "!?"

667
01:18:46,000 --> 01:18:51,000
*Koji whirls around, his light revealing Fuminori's expressionless face.*

668
01:18:51,000 --> 01:18:53,000
Fuminori: "You're trespassing."

669
01:18:53,000 --> 01:18:59,000
Koji: "S-so are you," Koji replies, barely managing to speak over the pounding of his heart.

670
01:18:59,000 --> 01:19:06,000
*Fuminori pushes past Koji and looks into the bathtub. He doesn't even flinch at the sight of the bones.*

671
01:19:06,000 --> 01:19:11,000
Fuminori: "A friend of mine lives here. I'm just running an errand."

672
01:19:11,000 --> 01:19:15,000
Koji: "What? Who is this friend? When did you meet them?"

673
01:19:15,000 --> 01:19:23,000
*Koji doesn't want to believe that the old, friendly Fuminori could have had contact with the denizens of this house.*

674
01:19:23,000 --> 01:19:31,000
Fuminori: "I'll introduce you one of these days," he says, turning to leave without even a glance at Koji. "I owe her my life."

675
01:19:31,000 --> 01:19:32,000
Koji: "Hey, Fuminori!"

676
01:19:32,000 --> 01:19:37,000
*Koji runs after Fuminori. His heart is finally beating normally again.*

677
01:19:37,000 --> 01:19:42,000
Koji: "Wait, is this friend of yours the reason you've been acting so strange?"

