856
01:37:04,000 --> 01:37:10,000
*I need to resolve once and for all to rid myself of the useless trappings of morality.*

857
01:37:10,000 --> 01:37:24,000
*Saya and I are all that matters. There's no point in worrying about what others think anymore -- although I suppose I should still talk to Saya's guardian, of course. I need to find Dr. Ogai as soon as possible.*

858
01:37:24,000 --> 01:37:32,000
*By the time I drift to sleep in exhaustion's comforting embrace, all doubts about Saya's actions have vanished from my mind.*

859
01:37:32,000 --> 01:37:36,000
*Whatever the case, all that matters is that she's returned to me.*

860
01:37:36,000 --> 01:37:41,000
*Two o'clock -- for Suzumi Yosuke, this is the most fulfilling time of day.*

861
01:37:41,000 --> 01:37:51,000
*After seeing his wife and daughter off, taking care of the morning chores, and eating a leisurely lunch, it's finally time to sit down at his easel.*

862
01:37:51,000 --> 01:38:06,000
*He's not a particularly popular painter, and he would only hold an exhibition if he were hurting for money. However, the design work he does on the side ensures that there's always enough to support his daily lifestyle.*

863
01:38:06,000 --> 01:38:17,000
*Alongside the salary his wife earns working for a magazine, they're able to pay their mortgage, send their daughter to school, and still have plenty left over.*

864
01:38:17,000 --> 01:38:21,000
*Yosuke's life is perfect -- leisurely and absent of want.*

865
01:38:21,000 --> 01:38:36,000
*He loves his house, considering it the symbol of his success. When he mows the lawn, polishes the windows and floors, and cleans the kitchen, toilet, and bath, he feels the same joy as he does when washing his own body.*

866
01:38:36,000 --> 01:39:04,000
Just as he knows the length of his fingernails and the time since his last meal, he also knows everything about his home's condition: the status of every door, the freshness of every flower, the amount of ice in the ice tray -- every last detail. This is his pride, and when he sits in his studio, smelling the turpentine and knowing that each element of his house is in perfect order, he feels the ultimate satisfaction.

867
01:39:04,000 --> 01:39:16,000
*While trying to find the right combination of paints on his palette, he suddenly feels thirsty, but soon remembers that there isn't much orange juice left in the refrigerator.*

868
01:39:16,000 --> 01:39:29,000
*In fact, it's also about time to stock up on bath additive and powdered soap. He could get everything at the supermarket when he goes to shop for dinner, but it will probably be quite heavy.*

869
01:39:29,000 --> 01:39:33,000
*((Now then, where should I leave off to go shopping?))*

870
01:39:33,000 --> 01:39:37,000
*As he ponders this dilemma, he heads downstairs to the kitchen.*

871
01:39:37,000 --> 01:39:44,000
*Just then, a breath of air tickles the back of his neck, bringing him to a halt in the middle of the hallway.*

872
01:39:44,000 --> 01:39:52,000
*A breeze -- impossible. Every window in the house is closed. Yosuke shut them himself during his morning cleaning.*

873
01:39:52,000 --> 01:39:57,000
*Yosuke enters the living room, searching for the source of the breeze.*

874
01:39:57,000 --> 01:40:11,000
*Something stinks. It's the same pungent smell of fetid swampland that emanates from the Sakisaka house. The window facing the yard next door is open, its curtains billowing loosely in the gentle breeze.*

875
01:40:11,000 --> 01:40:23,000
*There's a hole in the glass next to the lock. It looks strange, like it was melted by some chemical instead of broken. Someone must have reached through the hole to unlock the window.*

876
01:40:23,000 --> 01:40:28,000
*Yosuke stands paralyzed, his heart pounding with anger -- and fear.*

877
01:40:28,000 --> 01:40:39,000
*He listens carefully, but hears nothing. Perhaps the intruder has already finished his business and left... but a burglar wouldn't have left the room untouched, would he?*

878
01:40:39,000 --> 01:40:43,000
*Maybe he heard Yosuke coming and hid... somewhere nearby.*

879
01:40:43,000 --> 01:40:52,000
*Yosuke realizes that his still-wet palette knife is in his right hand. He must have forgotten to put it aside before going downstairs.*

880
01:40:52,000 --> 01:40:58,000
*He stares numbly at the knife for a moment, then decides that it's not enough protection.*

881
01:40:58,000 --> 01:41:07,000
*Instead, he grabs the ashtray sitting on top of the table. Made of thick, solid glass, it is big and heavy enough to serve as a weapon.*

882
01:41:07,000 --> 01:41:12,000
*The home that he thought of as part of himself now seems utterly alien.*

883
01:41:12,000 --> 01:41:27,000
*Keenly aware of the thumping of his heart, Yosuke looks around the living room and sees little that could be used as a hiding place. The intruder must have gone either to the guest room or through the dining room to the kitchen.*

884
01:41:27,000 --> 01:41:39,000
*The kitchen is close to the stairs. If there had been movement, Yosuke would have noticed it when he came down... which means that the guest room is the most likely place.*

885
01:41:39,000 --> 01:41:44,000
*He shuffles over to the guest room door and prepares to slide it open.*

886
01:41:44,000 --> 01:41:52,000
*But what is that stench? Could the breeze alone carry something so foul? It's as if the odor is coming from inside the room.*

887
01:41:52,000 --> 01:41:55,000
*He readies his ashtray and throws open the door.*

888
01:41:55,000 --> 01:42:02,000
*The straw-matted, Japanese-style room is empty. There is a closet, but no one could fit in there.*

889
01:42:02,000 --> 01:42:08,000
*So the intruder already left. Yosuke relaxes, the exhaustion of sudden relief coming over him.*

890
01:42:08,000 --> 01:42:11,000
*And that is when something seizes his ankle.*

891
01:42:11,000 --> 01:42:23,000
*The instant he freezes in shock, his leg is yanked out from under him, sending him crashing to the floor. Stars explode behind his eyes as his head smacks against the door rail.*

892
01:42:23,000 --> 01:42:32,000
*The hand -- if it can even be called that -- wrapped around Yosuke's ankle extends all the way back to beneath the living room sofa.*

893
01:42:32,000 --> 01:42:40,000
*There are barely five centimeters between the sofa and the floor, but the intruder is able to hide in that tiny space.*

894
01:42:40,000 --> 01:42:42,000
*It can't possibly be human.*

895
01:42:42,000 --> 01:42:43,000
Yosuke: "AHHHHHHH!"

896
01:42:43,000 --> 01:42:52,000
*Before the screaming Yosuke can regain his footing, countless hand-like appendages seize his arms and legs, rendering him helpless.*

897
01:42:52,000 --> 01:42:54,000
Saya:  sCarEd." atop him.

898
01:42:54,000 --> 01:42:58,000
Yosuke: "Yosuke can't even scream, his terror is so great.

899
01:42:58,000 --> 01:43:00,000
Saya:  sCarED. IT WOn't hURT."

900
01:43:00,000 --> 01:43:06,000
*Thin, tubelike appendages penetrate his ears and nose, wriggling deep into his skull.*

901
01:43:06,000 --> 01:43:11,000
*Right before the sensation drives him mad, Yosuke loses consciousness.*

902
01:43:11,000 --> 01:43:29,000
Koji: "Thank you for taking the time to see us," Koji says, his humble bow concealing his surprise at the doctor's youth. Even without her light makeup, she wouldn't look a day over thirty. She must be quite talented to be a leading neurosurgeon at such a young age.

903
01:43:29,000 --> 01:43:34,000
Ryoko: "Don't mention it. I was hoping somebody like you would come along."

904
01:43:34,000 --> 01:43:40,000
*Her friendly smile has none of the coldness one might expect from her sharp, refined beauty.*

905
01:43:40,000 --> 01:43:46,000
Ryoko: "It's a pleasure to meet you. I'm Dr. Tanbo, Sakisaka Fuminori's attending physician."

906
01:43:46,000 --> 01:43:50,000
Koji: "I'm Fuminori's friend Tonoh Koji. This is Tsukuba Yoh."

907
01:43:50,000 --> 01:43:53,000
*Yoh gives a quick bow, her expression apologetic.*

908
01:43:53,000 --> 01:44:07,000
*When they arrived at the T University Medical Center and asked to see Fuminori's doctor, Koji and Yoh had been prepared for rejection. They hadn't expected the ease with which their request was granted.*

909
01:44:07,000 --> 01:44:12,000
Ryoko: "You say you want to know what's wrong with him. Well, so do I."

910
01:44:12,000 --> 01:44:13,000
Koji: "I'm sorry?"

911
01:44:13,000 --> 01:44:20,000
Ryoko: "He didn't come in for his checkup two days ago. I tried calling his home, but there was no answer."

912
01:44:20,000 --> 01:44:31,000
*Two days ago... the same day Fuminori was searching that abandoned house. Koji frowns, wondering what was important enough for him to blow off his appointment.*

913
01:44:31,000 --> 01:44:33,000
Ryoko: "What is he like at school?"

914
01:44:33,000 --> 01:44:35,000
Koji: "He's... totally screwed up."

915
01:44:35,000 --> 01:44:42,000
*Seeing Yoh's shoulders jerk out of the corner of his eye, Koji regrets not choosing his words more carefully.*

916
01:44:42,000 --> 01:44:52,000
Koji: "Since the accident, he's been like a completely different person. We have no idea what to do. So we thought that talking to you might help."

917
01:44:52,000 --> 01:44:56,000
Ryoko: "Are you medical students too?" she asks out of nowhere.

918
01:44:56,000 --> 01:44:58,000
Koji: "Huh? Well, yes."

919
01:44:58,000 --> 01:45:01,000
Ryoko: "Would you like to see his charts?"

920
01:45:01,000 --> 01:45:05,000
Koji: "You'd really show them to us?" Koji replies, incredulous.

921
01:45:05,000 --> 01:45:09,000
*Dr. Tanbo regards him silently for a moment, then sighs and says,*

922
01:45:09,000 --> 01:45:10,000
Ryoko:

923
01:45:10,000 --> 01:45:14,000
Ryoko: "His files were stolen from the archives two nights ago."

924
01:45:14,000 --> 01:45:15,000
Koji: "What!?"

925
01:45:15,000 --> 01:45:21,000
*She stares hard at the astonished students, then shakes her head with a tired smile.*

926
01:45:21,000 --> 01:45:26,000
Ryoko: "Well, it doesn't look like you two were involved. That's a relief."

927
01:45:26,000 --> 01:45:28,000
Koji: "O-of course we weren't!"

928
01:45:28,000 --> 01:45:39,000
Ryoko: "However, the culprit must have had an interest in his condition -- or wanted to erase his records. Either way, I can only assume that it was someone close to him."

929
01:45:39,000 --> 01:45:40,000
Koji: "I see..."

930
01:45:40,000 --> 01:45:47,000
*An ominous thought flashes through Koji's mind -- it couldn't have been Fuminori himself, could it?*

931
01:45:47,000 --> 01:45:57,000
*Koji looks at Dr. Tanbo and finds her staring right back at him, her expression grave. He realizes that she must be harboring the same suspicion.*

932
01:45:57,000 --> 01:46:03,000
Ryoko: "What do you think? Do you have any idea who among his associates might have done it?"

933
01:46:03,000 --> 01:46:13,000
*Perhaps Dr. Tanbo didn't have anyone in mind when she asked, but Koji's thoughts immediately fly to the eerie house to which Fuminori led him.*

934
01:46:13,000 --> 01:46:21,000
Koji: "I don't really know what their relationship is, but there's someone called Ogai, probably a doctor or a..."

935
01:46:21,000 --> 01:46:27,000
*Koji stops speaking as he sees the dramatic change that has come across Dr. Tanbo's face.*

936
01:46:27,000 --> 01:46:29,000
Koji: "......You know Dr. Ogai?"

937
01:46:29,000 --> 01:46:34,000
Ryoko: "Do you know when and where Fuminori first encountered that man?"

938
01:46:34,000 --> 01:46:38,000
Koji: "No, that's what I'd like to know. Just who is this Ogai?"

939
01:46:38,000 --> 01:46:43,000
*After remaining silent for some time, Dr. Tanbo looses a heavy sigh.*

940
01:46:43,000 --> 01:46:57,000
Ryoko: "Alright. It's not like you couldn't find out on your own easily enough. Ogai Masahiko was a doctor teaching at this hospital. He was dismissed over six months ago, however, following certain incidents."

941
01:46:57,000 --> 01:47:00,000
Koji: "What incidents? What did he do?"

942
01:47:00,000 --> 01:47:05,000
Ryoko: "I can't say any more. And anyway, it has nothing to do with your friend."

943
01:47:05,000 --> 01:47:18,000
*Koji has no argument with which to answer Dr. Tanbo's flat rejection. However, he can't shake the feeling that this Ogai person is the key to unraveling the mystery surrounding Fuminori.*

944
01:47:18,000 --> 01:47:24,000
Koji: "Doctor," he says, making up his mind. "Fuminori might be... involved in a crime."

945
01:47:24,000 --> 01:47:29,000
*At this sudden declaration, both Yoh and Dr. Tanbo raise their eyebrows.*

946
01:47:29,000 --> 01:47:31,000
Ryoko: "What do you mean?"

947
01:47:31,000 --> 01:47:38,000
Koji: "A friend of ours went missing after going to see him. Fuminori denies any involvement, of course."

948
01:47:38,000 --> 01:47:40,000
Yoh: "You mean... Omi?"

949
01:47:40,000 --> 01:47:43,000
*Koji is unable to bear the shock in Yoh's voice.*

950
01:47:43,000 --> 01:47:46,000
Koji: "Sorry, Tsukuba... I couldn't tell you."

951
01:47:46,000 --> 01:47:51,000
*Dr. Tanbo is frowning, her expression even more serious than before.*

952
01:47:51,000 --> 01:48:06,000
Koji: "Right now, this Ogai seems to be the center of Fuminori's attention. If we know who he is and what Fuminori's looking for, we might start to see the whole picture. Please tell us, doctor. Just what happened at this hospital?"

953
01:48:06,000 --> 01:48:07,000
Ryoko: "......"

954
01:48:07,000 --> 01:48:14,000
*Dr. Tanbo hesitates for some time, refusing to make eye contact, but she finally shakes her head.*

955
01:48:14,000 --> 01:48:18,000
Ryoko: "I'm sorry. This is not a decision I can make on my own."

956
01:48:18,000 --> 01:48:19,000
Koji: "Doctor..."

957
01:48:19,000 --> 01:48:25,000
Ryoko: "Give me some time. I'll do my own investigating now that I know how far this has gone."

958
01:48:25,000 --> 01:48:26,000
Koji: "Please."

959
01:48:26,000 --> 01:48:35,000
*Koji is out of options. All that's left is to trust this young doctor. It's frustrating, but a friend's rights only go so far.*

960
01:48:35,000 --> 01:48:43,000
Ryoko: "Let's exchange cell phone numbers. I'll call you if I learn anything, and you call me the moment anything changes."

961
01:48:43,000 --> 01:48:44,000
Koji: "Alright."

962
01:48:44,000 --> 01:48:47,000
*((What the... What happened to me?))*

963
01:48:47,000 --> 01:48:52,000
*Yosuke's consciousness returns slowly, as though rising from a bog.*

964
01:48:52,000 --> 01:48:54,000
*He's cold... no, hot.*

965
01:48:54,000 --> 01:48:59,000
*Something itches, like tepid tongues and cold slugs crawling over his skin.*

966
01:48:59,000 --> 01:49:01,000
*((What the hell's going on?))*

967
01:49:01,000 --> 01:49:03,000
*Timidly, he opens his eyes.*

968
01:49:03,000 --> 01:49:04,000
Yosuke: "Wha..."

969
01:49:04,000 --> 01:49:05,000
*It's everywhere.*

970
01:49:05,000 --> 01:49:10,000
*The thing that attacked him in the living room -- it's everywhere!*

971
01:49:10,000 --> 01:49:12,000
*Terror shatters Yosuke's sanity.*

972
01:49:12,000 --> 01:49:14,000
Yosuke: "AHHHHHHHHHHH!"

973
01:49:14,000 --> 01:49:20,000
*He throws off the thing lying atop him, but his wild flailing sends him crashing to the floor.*

974
01:49:20,000 --> 01:49:29,000
*But is it really the floor? The long, wriggling fibers of what should be the carpet are winding themselves around his fingers.*

975
01:49:29,000 --> 01:49:31,000
*The floor is made of worms.*

976
01:49:31,000 --> 01:49:42,000
Yosuke: "He tears his limbs free of the worms and tries to stand, but loses his balance and tumbles to the floor again. The worms immediately swarm over his body.

977
01:49:42,000 --> 01:49:44,000
*((Where the hell am I!?))*

978
01:49:44,000 --> 01:49:46,000
*((Where did that thing take me!?))*

979
01:49:46,000 --> 01:49:52,000
*Yosuke crawls across the worm-ridden floor towards the only exit from the pulsating room.*

980
01:49:52,000 --> 01:49:59,000
*When he gets outside, however, all he can see is blood, bile, and rotten meat. There is no place to run.*

981
01:49:59,000 --> 01:50:01,000
Yosuke: "What is this!?"

982
01:50:01,000 --> 01:50:12,000
*Most terrifying of all, this hellish place has the same layout as Yosuke's house. In a half-mad daze, he wanders through the nightmarish mockery of his home.*

983
01:50:12,000 --> 01:50:25,000
*In the small room where his studio should be, he finds an easel made of bones displaying a blood-soaked canvas. Like some cruel joke, everything is exactly where it would be in Yosuke's studio.*

984
01:50:25,000 --> 01:50:28,000
Yosuke: "Dammit, let me out! Let me out of here!!"

985
01:50:28,000 --> 01:50:32,000
*Howling, Yosuke lashes out against everything within reach.*

986
01:50:32,000 --> 01:50:36,000
*The easel of bone shatters, driving splinters into his fist.*

987
01:50:36,000 --> 01:50:43,000
*He feels the pain, but does not wake from the nightmare. If this isn't a dream, then what is it?*

988
01:50:43,000 --> 01:50:51,000
*When his strength gives out, Yosuke falls to his knees, sobbing. For the first time in his life, he prays to the gods.*

989
01:50:51,000 --> 01:50:55,000
*The sound of the door opening and closing grates on his ears.*

990
01:50:55,000 --> 01:50:59,000
*((Downstairs... the front door? Someone else is here?))*

991
01:50:59,000 --> 01:51:00,000
Wife: "wE'RE hOmE!"

992
01:51:00,000 --> 01:51:06,000
*Yosuke trembles at the bloodcurdling sound. It's that thing again; the monster has returned.*

993
01:51:06,000 --> 01:51:09,000
Hiromi: "DadDY, wE'RE hoMe! WhERe's DiNnER?"

994
01:51:09,000 --> 01:51:12,000
Wife: "OH, hE'S nOt HeRE? dID hE go ShOPpInG?"

995
01:51:12,000 --> 01:51:14,000
Hiromi: "WHEn cAN we eAt?"

996
01:51:14,000 --> 01:51:27,000
*Yosuke hears the sound of something slimy sloshing its way up the stairs. Even as he cowers in terror, he slides his trembling hand across the floor and grabs one of the bones from the broken easel.*

997
01:51:27,000 --> 01:51:37,000
*The tip of the bone is nice and sharp. If he holds it in both hands and puts his weight behind it, he might be able to use it to defend himself.*

998
01:51:37,000 --> 01:51:39,000
Wife: "HonEY, aRe YOu hoMe?"

999
01:51:39,000 --> 01:51:47,000
*The monster's growls are getting closer. Holding his breath, Yosuke presses his back against the wall next to the door.*

1000
01:51:47,000 --> 01:52:00,000
*The pounding of his heart is like thunder in his ears, so loud that he fears the creature might hear it. He knows it will eat him if it finds him again, but it's all he can do to keep from crying.*

1001
01:52:00,000 --> 01:52:02,000
*At last, the door creaks open...*

1002
01:52:02,000 --> 01:52:03,000
Wife: "HONEy?"

1003
01:52:03,000 --> 01:52:10,000
Yosuke: "Yosuke leaps on the creature as it enters, fear turning his roar into a high-pitched scream.

1004
01:52:10,000 --> 01:52:19,000
*The flesh-beast is covered in sludge and vile juices, but before horror can paralyze him, Yosuke brings his bone-stake stabbing down.*

1005
01:52:19,000 --> 01:52:28,000
Wife: "The monster screams as the stake pierces its chest and punches through to the other side. It falls back, writhing in agony.

1006
01:52:28,000 --> 01:52:31,000
*The sight of its pain sets Yosuke's blood on fire.*

1007
01:52:31,000 --> 01:52:37,000
*((I can win. I can kill it! If I finish it off before it enters my head again, I'm safe!))*

1008
01:52:37,000 --> 01:52:48,000
Yosuke: "Yosuke grabs the bone and twists with all his might. The monster convulses and gurgles, its trembling tentacles reaching up as though begging for help.

1009
01:52:48,000 --> 01:52:50,000
Yosuke: "Die! Die! DIE!"

1010
01:52:50,000 --> 01:53:00,000
*Yosuke knocks it to the floor, then brings his heel crashing down on its flopping body again and again. With each stomp, its groans and spasms grow weaker.*

1011
01:53:00,000 --> 01:53:08,000
*When the monster at last stops twitching, Yosuke, panting hard, tears the stake from its corpse and rises to his feet.*

1012
01:53:08,000 --> 01:53:11,000
Hiromi: "......DadDY?" something squeals.

1013
01:53:11,000 --> 01:53:17,000
*Yosuke turns around to see another, smaller monster peeking out at him from the stair landing.*

1014
01:53:17,000 --> 01:53:19,000
*((There's still one left.))*

1015
01:53:19,000 --> 01:53:28,000
*His desperate, rage-filled attack both exhilarated him and gave him a taste for violence. This one will be easier; it's smaller and weaker.*

1016
01:53:28,000 --> 01:53:34,000
*Grinning maniacally, Yosuke raises his stake and moves towards the second creature.*

1017
01:53:34,000 --> 01:53:38,000
Hiromi: "The monster flees screaming down the stairs.

1018
01:53:38,000 --> 01:53:48,000
*Not about to let his prey escape, Yosuke roars and gives chase. The thought that killing the monsters might end this nightmare feeds his savage bloodlust.*

1019
01:53:48,000 --> 01:53:50,000
Hiromi: "NO, DaDdy! nO!"

1020
01:53:50,000 --> 01:54:10,000
*When the monster trips and falls in the dining room, Yosuke leaps on top of it and brings the stake crashing down. His bloodlust unsated, he pulls it free, then drives it again into the monster's flesh -- once, twice, thrice, and more -- until there is nothing left but shredded, pulverized meat.*

1021
01:54:10,000 --> 01:54:15,000
*Eventually, the only sound in the house is Yosuke's heavy breathing.*

1022
01:54:15,000 --> 01:54:20,000
*He has slain two monsters, but the nightmare shows no sign of ending.*

1023
01:54:20,000 --> 01:54:24,000
*Yosuke staggers to the front door and goes outside.*

1024
01:54:24,000 --> 01:54:26,000
Yosuke: "Hahahahahahaha..."

1025
01:54:26,000 --> 01:54:29,000
*The sky, the city -- everything has gone mad.*

1026
01:54:29,000 --> 01:54:32,000
*Twisted shapes, nauseating colors, stinking air.*

1027
01:54:32,000 --> 01:54:35,000
*There is no escape. No end to the nightmare.*

1028
01:54:35,000 --> 01:54:40,000
*The last remnant of Yosuke's sanity vanishes like dust in the wind.*

1029
01:54:40,000 --> 01:54:41,000
Saya: "Hi, mister."

1030
01:54:41,000 --> 01:54:44,000
*Yosuke turns to the sound of a young girl's voice.*

1031
01:54:44,000 --> 01:54:56,000
*She is standing in front of the house next door, wearing a spotless one piece over her pure white skin. In the midst of this filth-ridden world, she alone glows with beauty.*

1032
01:54:56,000 --> 01:54:58,000
