02:49:37,000 --> 02:49:38,000
Koji:  her."

1556
02:49:38,000 --> 02:49:46,000
Fuminori: "Oh," Fuminori replies curtly, still staring into the distance. "That's not good. I wonder what happened to her."

1557
02:49:46,000 --> 02:49:47,000
Koji: "......"

1558
02:49:47,000 --> 02:49:58,000
*Fuminori's tone is completely emotionless. Koji might as well have asked him about the weather or the condition of the mountain roads near their destination.*

1559
02:49:58,000 --> 02:50:04,000
Koji: "I asked you this before, but you're sure you don't have any idea what happened to her?"

1560
02:50:04,000 --> 02:50:13,000
Fuminori: "Not a clue," Fuminori answers, in exactly the same tone that he used when Koji first questioned him following Omi's disappearance.

1561
02:50:13,000 --> 02:50:17,000
Koji: "Koji's eyes narrow. "It's like you don't give a damn."

1562
02:50:17,000 --> 02:50:31,000
Fuminori: "That's not true." Finally Fuminori shows some emotion. He sounds hurt, like he can't believe Koji could think such a thing. "She disappeared on the way to my place, didn't she? Of course I'm worried."

1563
02:50:31,000 --> 02:50:39,000
*Sudden frustration wells up inside Koji. If possible, he'd like nothing more than to beat the secrets out of Fuminori's head.*

1564
02:50:39,000 --> 02:50:51,000
*Koji is worried sick about Omi. To have his concern brushed off so coldly would be unbearable coming from a complete stranger; but from Fuminori, who was his best friend, it's...*

1565
02:50:51,000 --> 02:51:00,000
*Fuminori never used to be this callous. Even if Koji tried to interrogate him, he'd probably never find out what changed him so.*

1566
02:51:00,000 --> 02:51:20,000
*If Fuminori were still just hiding inside the shell he'd erected around himself after the accident, Koji might have been able to get some answers out of him. With this sly, evasive Fuminori, however, there's nothing Koji can do. Fuminori will never reveal his true intentions -- not to anyone.*

1567
02:51:20,000 --> 02:51:25,000
*All that's left, then, is for Koji to discover the truth on his own.*

1568
02:51:25,000 --> 02:51:29,000
Koji: "Omi was going to talk to you about Tsukuba, you know."

1569
02:51:29,000 --> 02:51:30,000
Fuminori: "Oh?"

1570
02:51:30,000 --> 02:51:42,000
*Fuminori smiles bitterly at the mention of Tsukuba's name, perhaps feeling sympathy for her pain. To Koji, however, it seems like pity, the sort one directs at an ant or a worm.*

1571
02:51:42,000 --> 02:51:49,000
Fuminori: "I wouldn't know what to say. To be honest, it's been hard to talk to her after what happened."

1572
02:51:49,000 --> 02:51:50,000
Koji: "......"

1573
02:51:50,000 --> 02:51:51,000
*Unbelievable.*

1574
02:51:51,000 --> 02:52:04,000
*If Fuminori's feelings for Yoh were really this cold, then he would have rejected her when she first confessed to him. But he didn't -- or at least, the Fuminori before the accident didn't.*

1575
02:52:04,000 --> 02:52:15,000
*Once again, Koji can't help but wonder if this man who looks like his friend is really a different person who only possesses the memories of Sakisaka Fuminori.*

1576
02:52:15,000 --> 02:52:29,000
*The snow has stopped falling when they get off the West Nasu Flats Interchange. This area must already be getting a lot of snow, however, as the nearby mountains are covered in white beneath the trees.*

1577
02:52:29,000 --> 02:52:39,000
*By the time they turn off the highway and enter the mountains, road conditions are already bad enough for Koji to regret having forgotten tire chains.*

1578
02:52:39,000 --> 02:52:46,000
*Nevertheless, he continues to power his Accord up the precarious slopes with only a road map to guide him.*

1579
02:52:46,000 --> 02:53:01,000
*In places like this, an address isn't enough to pinpoint a location. His only choice is to drive down every road, including private roads that aren't even on the map, while searching for something that matches the photograph.*

1580
02:53:01,000 --> 02:53:04,000
Koji: "Who would buy a home in a place like this?"

1581
02:53:04,000 --> 02:53:09,000
Fuminori: "It's far from prying eyes. That must be why Dr. Ogai chose it."

1582
02:53:09,000 --> 02:53:10,000
Koji: "......"

1583
02:53:10,000 --> 02:53:14,000
*The more he hears about Ogai, the less Koji wants to meet him.*

1584
02:53:14,000 --> 02:53:19,000
*Fuminori is the one who spots the narrow road half-hidden in the trees.*

1585
02:53:19,000 --> 02:53:27,000
*It's practically an animal trail, overgrown with weeds that are tall and strong enough to withstand the weight of the snow.*

1586
02:53:27,000 --> 02:53:29,000
Koji: "Is this really a road?"

1587
02:53:29,000 --> 02:53:40,000
*Koji stops the car and sticks his head out of the window to stare into the dark forest, but he can't see where the path leads through the tightly-packed trees.*

1588
02:53:40,000 --> 02:53:42,000
Fuminori: "How does it look to you?"

1589
02:53:42,000 --> 02:53:49,000
*Fuminori hands Koji the photo, which he compares to the mountain ridges visible beyond the trees.*

1590
02:53:49,000 --> 02:53:52,000
Koji: "Yeah, it's definitely the right angle."

1591
02:53:52,000 --> 02:53:54,000
Fuminori: "Let's check it out."

1592
02:53:54,000 --> 02:54:02,000
*Fuminori's tone is as flat as always, but there is a quiet intensity in his voice that leaves no room for argument.*

1593
02:54:02,000 --> 02:54:14,000
*Although Koji is worried that his car's suspension won't be able to handle the terrain, there's no turning back now. He shifts into second and starts down the frozen road.*

1594
02:54:14,000 --> 02:54:24,000
*The sun sets early at high altitudes. As the car creeps up the mountain path, Koji catches glimpses through the trees of the gradually darkening sky.*

1595
02:54:24,000 --> 02:54:38,000
*The forest is completely still, with no sound save for the rumble of the Accord's engine and the crackle of snow and brush beneath its tires. Fuminori is once again staring silently through the front window.*

1596
02:54:38,000 --> 02:54:51,000
*In the ominous silence, Koji feels the same faint chill that he felt when standing before Ogai's suburban home. It feels wrong, as though he is traveling deeper and deeper into a world not his own.*

1597
02:54:51,000 --> 02:54:58,000
*After some time, a blocky shape suddenly appears amid the trees, standing out against the twilight sky.*

1598
02:54:58,000 --> 02:54:59,000
Koji: "......"

1599
02:54:59,000 --> 02:55:07,000
*Koji turns off the engine and compares the structure in front of him to the picture in his hand -- a perfect match.*

1600
02:55:07,000 --> 02:55:13,000
*Before he can tell Fuminori, however, his silent friend is already out of the car.*

1601
02:55:13,000 --> 02:55:14,000
Koji: "Hey!"

1602
02:55:14,000 --> 02:55:26,000
*Realizing that it's pointless to call out to him, Koji shakes his head, grabs the flashlight from the glove compartment, and follows Fuminori across the snow-covered yard.*

1603
02:55:26,000 --> 02:55:36,000
*The photo must not have been taken recently, as the old, run-down cabin before them has clearly been left to the mercy of the elements for some time.*

1604
02:55:36,000 --> 02:55:47,000
*The front door appears to be locked, but Fuminori kicks it down without a second thought. Koji just watches, knowing that nothing he could say now would matter.*

1605
02:55:47,000 --> 02:55:53,000
*All of the windows are shut with heavy curtains, and the gloom inside is thick and stifling.*

1606
02:55:53,000 --> 02:56:01,000
*Fuminori turns on his own flashlight and starts rummaging through the cabin without regard for its owner's privacy.*

1607
02:56:01,000 --> 02:56:16,000
*Koji is reluctant to do the same, but it is obvious that this mountain retreat has been abandoned for a long time, just like the house in Tokyo. There's no point in being considerate now. He goes to search a different room.*

1608
02:56:16,000 --> 02:56:22,000
*Soon after entering the cabin, however, he realizes that their search is meaningless.*

1609
02:56:22,000 --> 02:56:31,000
*There's nothing inside but the bare necessities of life. Some rooms are even completely empty, save for a thick layer of dust on the floor.*

1610
02:56:31,000 --> 02:56:46,000
*Of what few pieces of furniture are present, more than half appear to have never been used. There's an empty chest of drawers without a single scratch or handprint, but bearing the telltale signs of mold and moisture damage.*

1611
02:56:46,000 --> 02:56:58,000
*The condition of the cabin is eerie, though in a different way than the filthiness of the house in the city. It's like someone put together a mockup of a home and then left it to decay.*

1612
02:56:58,000 --> 02:57:05,000
*The only signs that anyone lived here are found in the toilet, the bath, the kitchen, and the bedroom.*

1613
02:57:05,000 --> 02:57:10,000
*It appears that the cabin was never used for anything but eating and sleeping.*

1614
02:57:10,000 --> 02:57:26,000
*Beneath the darkened sky, the snow itself seems to glow with a cold, white light. The scene is like something out of a fairytale, but to Koji it serves only as an unpleasant reminder that he has stepped outside of the reality that he knows.*

1615
02:57:26,000 --> 02:57:38,000
*Next to the front porch is a plain wooden door half buried in the ground. It's locked, of course, but Koji sees no reason for restraint after what Fuminori did to the front door.*

1616
02:57:38,000 --> 02:57:49,000
*The door offers surprisingly little resistance to Koji's heavy kick, breaking open to reveal a set of concrete stairs leading down into a pitch-black basement.*

1617
02:57:49,000 --> 02:57:50,000
Koji: "......"

1618
02:57:50,000 --> 02:57:58,000
*Koji would prefer to leave such a forbidding place to Fuminori, but it's not like he can just ask him to take his place.*

1619
02:57:58,000 --> 02:58:04,000
*He descends into the chilly darkness, the beam of his flashlight leading the way.*

1620
02:58:04,000 --> 02:58:14,000
*There turns out to be nothing in the basement but a storage room and a boiler, exactly what one would expect to find in an isolated mountain cabin.*

1621
02:58:14,000 --> 02:58:25,000
*The few packages of preserved food sitting on the shelves have long since passed their expiration dates, and the boiler doesn't appear to have been used in years.*

1622
02:58:25,000 --> 02:58:31,000
*Koji guesses that Ogai's mountain home has been abandoned longer than the house in Tokyo.*

1623
02:58:31,000 --> 02:58:38,000
*Was Fuminori simply mistaken when he said that Ogai might be here? Or was he lying from the beginning?*

1624
02:58:38,000 --> 02:58:47,000
*Not sure what to do next, Koji goes back up the stairs and walks around the outside of the cabin -- and there he finds the backyard.*

1625
02:58:47,000 --> 02:58:58,000
*It's in much worse condition than the front yard, having been mostly reclaimed by the forest. It must have been neglected even when the cabin was still in use.*

1626
02:58:58,000 --> 02:59:14,000
*The remnants of a woodshed lie in the yard, the mushrooms growing on it speaking to how much time has passed since its collapse. Next to the rotten logs, however, stands a circle of stone that has not yet succumbed to the elements.*

1627
02:59:14,000 --> 02:59:15,000
*A well.*

1628
02:59:15,000 --> 02:59:29,000
*The well has no bucket or pulley, and when Koji peers carefully into it, he sees that the water is no longer flowing. It's probably less than ten meters deep, depending on how much mud is piled up inside.*

1629
02:59:29,000 --> 02:59:34,000
*Koji's search of the cabin has revealed nothing of interest, inside or out.*

1630
02:59:34,000 --> 02:59:43,000
*Leaning against the edge of the well, Koji wonders why Ogai bought this remote home deep in the mountains, and what he was doing here.*

1631
02:59:43,000 --> 02:59:49,000
*As far as Koji can tell, there's no sign that more than one person ever stayed here.*

1632
02:59:49,000 --> 02:59:52,000
Fuminori: "It's far from prying eyes."

1633
02:59:52,000 --> 03:00:08,000
*Fuminori's words play back in Koji's head. Could this have been some sort of secret refuge, a place to remain hidden from the world? That would explain why there's nothing to suggest that whoever lived here did anything more than eat and sleep.*

1634
03:00:08,000 --> 03:00:15,000
*Koji suddenly remembers the doctor he met yesterday at T University. Maybe she'd know something.*

1635
03:00:15,000 --> 03:00:23,000
*He takes out his phone and calls up the newly-stored number. There's barely a signal, but it manages to get through.*

1636
03:00:23,000 --> 03:00:29,000
*Koji's hopes are soon dashed, however, when his call goes straight to Dr. Tanbo's voice mail.*

1637
03:00:29,000 --> 03:00:42,000
*He considers calling back later, but realizes that it would be hard to talk to her with Fuminori around. Fuminori would not at all be pleased to learn that Koji and Yoh went to see his doctor.*

1638
03:00:42,000 --> 03:00:48,000
*Koji decides that he'd better tell the doctor what he can while he's still alone.*

1639
03:00:48,000 --> 03:00:53,000
Koji: "Hello, this is Tonoh Koji. Thank you for your help yesterday."

1640
03:00:53,000 --> 03:01:06,000
*Koji leaves a clear and concise message, explaining that he went with Fuminori to Ogai's mountain retreat, giving the address, and asking for confirmation that the property belongs to Ogai.*

1641
03:01:06,000 --> 03:01:10,000
Koji: "I'll call again when I get back to Tokyo. Goodbye."

1642
03:01:10,000 --> 03:01:23,000
*After hanging up, Koji thinks back to their visit to the hospital. Is Dr. Tanbo actually investigating like she said she would? Her reluctance to speak of Dr. Ogai is weighing on his mind.*

1643
03:01:23,000 --> 03:01:31,000
*He talked to Yoh about it on the way home, but they were unable to decide whether the doctor could really be trusted.*

1644
03:01:31,000 --> 03:01:35,000
*Speaking of which, how is Yoh doing? Koji hasn't seen her today.*

1645
03:01:35,000 --> 03:01:43,000
*He didn't say a word to her about his trip to Tochigi. She might be worried, especially so soon after Omi's disappearance.*

1646
03:01:43,000 --> 03:01:51,000
*Thinking to check up on her, Koji dials Yoh's number... and is surprised when it rings longer than it usually does.*

1647
03:01:51,000 --> 03:01:53,000
*Did she forget her phone somewhere?*

1648
03:01:53,000 --> 03:01:56,000
*Just as he's about to give up, the call connects.*

1649
03:01:56,000 --> 03:02:08,000
*The first thing Koji hears is a strange sound. It's not signal interference, but some kind of wet, distorted noise -- like the voiceless groans, or perhaps sobs, of someone far away.*

1650
03:02:08,000 --> 03:02:13,000
Yoh: "No, that's exactly what they are. The person on the other side is crying.

1651
03:02:13,000 --> 03:02:15,000
Koji: "T-Tsukuba? Is that you!?"

1652
03:02:15,000 --> 03:02:17,000
Yoh: "Who's... there..."

1653
03:02:17,000 --> 03:02:24,000
*There's a response, but is it really Tsukuba's voice? It's too twisted with agony for Koji to tell.*

1654
03:02:24,000 --> 03:02:29,000
*Panic surges through Koji as he realizes that something is terribly wrong.*

1655
03:02:29,000 --> 03:02:34,000
Koji: "It's Koji, Tonoh Koji! Is that you, Tsukuba? Where are you!?"

1656
03:02:34,000 --> 03:02:44,000
Yoh: "After a short period of nothing but pained moans, words start coming through the speaker one by one, as though each takes an act of will.

1657
03:02:44,000 --> 03:02:51,000
Yoh: "I was... attacked... by a monster... and now... there's... something wrong... with my... body..."

1658
03:02:51,000 --> 03:02:54,000
Koji: "What!? What happened!? Are you alright!?"

1659
03:02:54,000 --> 03:03:05,000
*Yoh must be delirious, because Koji can't understand a thing she's saying. Her gasps and wheezes, however, are enough to tell him that she's in unimaginable pain.*

1660
03:03:05,000 --> 03:03:11,000
Yoh: "I'm... rotting away... my skin... is melting... my... ear just... came off..."

1661
03:03:11,000 --> 03:03:16,000
*She's not making any sense! Koji feels despair seize his heart in an iron grip.*

1662
03:03:16,000 --> 03:03:20,000
*What is happening to Yoh now, a hundred kilometers away?*

1663
03:03:20,000 --> 03:03:26,000
*Only her voice gives any hint of what she's going through. There's nothing he can do for her.*

1664
03:03:26,000 --> 03:03:32,000
Yoh: "Help me... Koji... This... this isn't... how my... fingers... are supposed... to look..."

1665
03:03:32,000 --> 03:03:35,000
Koji: "Call the cops, Tsukuba! Call for help!"

1666
03:03:35,000 --> 03:03:39,000
Yoh: "No! I can't... let anyone... see me... like this..."

1667
03:03:39,000 --> 03:03:46,000
*Yoh suddenly breaks into a violent hacking cough, as though trying to expel something filling her throat.*

1668
03:03:46,000 --> 03:03:47,000
Koji: "Tsukuba!!"

1669
03:03:47,000 --> 03:03:52,000
*Koji screams into the phone, his reason overwhelmed by unimaginable horror.*

1670
03:03:52,000 --> 03:04:03,000
*Which is why he is unable to react when the phone is suddenly knocked from his hand, and also why he didn't notice Fuminori sneaking up on him until it was too late.*

1671
03:04:03,000 --> 03:04:04,000
Koji: "Wha--"

1672
03:04:04,000 --> 03:04:26,000
*Fuminori seizes Koji's lower jaw with his right hand, cutting off Koji's angry shout. Koji can hardly believe the strength of the smaller man's grip. His biggest mistake was leaning back against the well. There is nothing to grab onto as Fuminori pushes him backwards over the edge. He can only flail his arms vainly against the air.*

1673
03:04:26,000 --> 03:04:29,000
*Koji soon loses his balance entirely.*

1674
03:04:29,000 --> 03:04:40,000
*He feels a terrifying weightlessness as the world spins before his eyes. Before he can realize what has happened, his back strikes something with tremendous force.*

1675
03:04:40,000 --> 03:04:53,000
*He thrashes wildly as cold, dirty water fills his mouth and freezes him to the core. Only when his fingers find the wall of the well is he able to regain his sense of direction and right himself.*

1676
03:04:53,000 --> 03:04:58,000
*On his hands and knees in the mud, Koji vomits filthy water out of his lungs.*

1677
03:04:58,000 --> 03:05:06,000
Koji: "Fuminori..." he tries to shout, but it comes out as a hoarse groan, distorted by the echo in the cramped space.

1678
03:05:06,000 --> 03:05:11,000
Fuminori: "Fuminori's laughter, on the other hand, is crystal clear.

1679
03:05:11,000 --> 03:05:17,000
Fuminori: "Sorry for interrupting your call," he says scornfully. "Here, I'll return this."

1680
03:05:17,000 --> 03:05:28,000
*Fuminori tosses Koji's phone into the well. Koji catches it just before it hits him in the face, but finds that the battery pack has been removed, rendering it useless.*

1681
03:05:28,000 --> 03:05:30,000
Koji: "What the hell are you doing!?"

1682
03:05:30,000 --> 03:05:36,000
*This is no joke. It's a miracle that Koji is uninjured. He could easily have broken his neck.*

1683
03:05:36,000 --> 03:05:40,000
*And just because he's not hurt doesn't mean that he's safe.*

1684
03:05:40,000 --> 03:05:53,000
*Koji feels around the inside of the well, searching for something to hold on to, but the mud-covered stone offers no purchase. It's obvious that he won't be able to get out without help.*

1685
03:05:53,000 --> 03:06:00,000
Fuminori: "Too bad the fall didn't kill you. Now you have to freeze to death. You really have no luck, Koji."

1686
03:06:00,000 --> 03:06:08,000
Koji: "You can't be serious..." Koji starts to say, but trails off as the pieces finally come together in his head.

1687
03:06:08,000 --> 03:06:20,000
*Today's sudden change in Fuminori's attitude -- that smile that always seemed somehow malevolent. Fuminori hadn't been smiling at Koji, but at the thought of his friend's death.*

1688
03:06:20,000 --> 03:06:21,000
Koji: "Why!?"

1689
03:06:21,000 --> 03:06:27,000
*He can't wrap his head around this turn of events. Why would Fuminori try to kill him?*

1690
03:06:27,000 --> 03:06:34,000
*True, Fuminori had wanted Koji to stay out of his business, but is that really a motive for murder?*

1691
03:06:34,000 --> 03:06:46,000
Fuminori: "It's not that I needed you dead right now, exactly, but you might have become trouble later on. So I figured I might as well take advantage of this remote location to, well..."

1692
03:06:46,000 --> 03:06:49,000
Koji: "Might as well? You're doing this on a whim!?"

1693
03:06:49,000 --> 03:07:05,000
Fuminori: "Do you really need a reason to die?" Fuminori replies coldly. He sounds truly amazed that Koji would ask such a thing. "What makes you so special, Koji? People die for no reason at all. My parents did, and I almost followed them."

1694
03:07:05,000 --> 03:07:06,000
Koji: "You're crazy!"

1695
03:07:06,000 --> 03:07:12,000
Fuminori: "Come up with your own reason, why don't you? You'll have plenty of time down there."

1696
03:07:12,000 --> 03:07:20,000
*Fuminori disappears from view, leaving Koji alone in the darkness with nothing to connect him to the outside world.*

1697
03:07:20,000 --> 03:07:22,000
Koji: "Fuminori! Hey! Fuminori!!"

1698
03:07:22,000 --> 03:07:36,000
*Koji shouts at the top of his lungs, knowing beyond a doubt that if Fuminori leaves, all hope of rescue will vanish with him. No one will ever hear him calling for help from the bottom of this mountain well.*

1699
03:07:36,000 --> 03:07:42,000
Koji: "It's Tsukuba! She's in trouble! Hey, Fuminori! Listen! Get me out of here!!"

1700
03:07:42,000 --> 03:07:48,000
*In his desperation, Koji no longer comprehends the futility of begging for mercy.*

1701
03:07:48,000 --> 03:07:58,000
*No god or devil will answer him. His only hope is that Fuminori will have a change of heart. Praying for a miracle, he keeps calling Fuminori's name.*

1702
03:07:58,000 --> 03:08:11,000
*Eventually, the sky grows as dark as the bottom of the well. Koji can no longer make out the edge of the opening, and he has long since lost track of how many hours he has been screaming.*

1703
03:08:11,000 --> 03:08:18,000
*Nevertheless, he continues to scream, for he knows that the despair silence brings will kill him.*

1704
03:08:18,000 --> 03:08:26,000
*I feel great, the same feeling that you get when the last piece of a difficult puzzle slides smoothly into place.*

1705
03:08:26,000 --> 03:08:29,000
*I have killed a man, and no one will ever know.*

1706
03:08:29,000 --> 03:08:39,000
*It is a long way back to civilization, but neither the cold nor the exhaustion can ruin my good mood as I walk alone down the snow-covered mountain road.*

1707
03:08:39,000 --> 03:08:49,000
*I was tempted to use Koji's car, but that would have introduced a flaw into the plan. I don't want anyone to connect me to his disappearance.*

1708
03:08:49,000 --> 03:09:13,000
*The plan formed in my mind the moment that I realized how remote the location was. Even if I couldn't find anything to lead me to Dr. Ogai, his absence would at least prove that the cabin had been utterly abandoned -- in which case, it would be the perfect spot to take care of a problem. I knew coming all the way out to Tochigi wouldn't be a waste of time.*

1709
03:09:13,000 --> 03:09:31,000
*I didn't even need to use the meat cleaver hidden under my jacket. A dry well -- it's like fate itself provided me with the perfect setting. That idiot didn't even realize the danger he was in, and his phone call distracted him enough for me to take him by surprise.*

1710
03:09:31,000 --> 03:09:42,000
*Now one of the two people whose questions might have caused trouble for me and Saya has vanished from the face of the Earth. All that's left is to eliminate the other.*

1711
03:09:42,000 --> 03:09:54,000
*Tsukuba Yoh -- I mustn't underestimate her just because she's less aggressive than Koji. Even she should be able to see a connection between the disappearances of her two friends.*

1712
03:09:54,000 --> 03:10:07,000
*I suppose I should be thankful that it was Yoh to whom Koji was talking on the phone. If he'd reported our location to a third party, I'd have to track down and eliminate that person too.*

1713
03:10:07,000 --> 03:10:22,000
