2062
03:46:08,000 --> 03:46:18,000
*There's no trace of the bookish, mild-mannered woman Koji met at the hospital. Her expression is now set in a hard mask, and her eyes are sharp and wary.*

2063
03:46:18,000 --> 03:46:33,000
*In the darkness at the bottom of the well, it is possible -- however unlikely -- that the change in her features is due to the ominous shadows cast by her lamp. It's not so easy, however, to explain the change in her demeanor.*

2064
03:46:33,000 --> 03:46:35,000
Koji: "Um... why are you here?"

2065
03:46:35,000 --> 03:46:50,000
Ryoko: "You called me, didn't you?" Ryoko replies brusquely, glaring at Koji like an annoyed professor. "I tried calling back, but you didn't answer. Neither did your friend Tsukuba. Am I supposed to think everything's fine?"

2066
03:46:50,000 --> 03:46:51,000
Koji: "N-no, but..."

2067
03:46:51,000 --> 03:47:00,000
*Koji still doesn't understand why she acted so quickly, but it's a different part of what she just said that seizes his attention.*

2068
03:47:00,000 --> 03:47:03,000
Koji: "Wait, Tsukuba!? You called her too?"

2069
03:47:03,000 --> 03:47:10,000
Ryoko: "Like I said, she didn't pick up either. To be honest, I figured you were both corpses already."

2070
03:47:10,000 --> 03:47:11,000
Koji: "......"

2071
03:47:11,000 --> 03:47:17,000
*That's right. He almost died, and at the hands of the man he thought was his best friend.*

2072
03:47:17,000 --> 03:47:26,000
*Anger and frustration well up inside of him. He can't forgive Fuminori's betrayal; nor can he forgive himself for his foolishness.*

2073
03:47:26,000 --> 03:47:33,000
*And now he has no idea if Tsukuba is safe. Fuminori tried to kill Koji. Could he have done the same to her?*

2074
03:47:33,000 --> 03:47:43,000
Ryoko: "Calm down, why don't you?" Ryoko says irritably, turning away to examine the inside of the well. "There's nothing you can do from here."

2075
03:47:43,000 --> 03:47:51,000
Koji: "If you thought something was wrong," Koji says to her back, "then you must have called the police, right?"

2076
03:47:51,000 --> 03:47:52,000
Ryoko: "The police?"

2077
03:47:52,000 --> 03:47:58,000
*Still engrossed in her examination of the walls, Ryoko laughs scornfully at the idea.*

2078
03:47:58,000 --> 03:48:02,000
Ryoko: "So you still think that's the way out, do you?"

2079
03:48:02,000 --> 03:48:04,000
Koji: "What's that supposed to mean?"

2080
03:48:04,000 --> 03:48:14,000
*Annoyed by her condescending attitude, Koji is about to demand answers when she cuts him off with a gesture and shines her light at a corner of the well.*

2081
03:48:14,000 --> 03:48:17,000
Ryoko: "You didn't notice this, Tonoh?"

2082
03:48:17,000 --> 03:48:18,000
Koji: "Huh?"

2083
03:48:18,000 --> 03:48:28,000
*In the light of the lamp, Koji sees that some of the stones are a different shade than the rest of the wall. This must be what Ryoko was looking for.*

2084
03:48:28,000 --> 03:48:31,000
Koji: "Huh? No, there wasn't enough light."

2085
03:48:31,000 --> 03:48:32,000
Ryoko: "Hmm..."

2086
03:48:32,000 --> 03:48:43,000
*Ryoko's gaze moves slowly along the wall, finally coming to rest on a gap between two of the stones. The hole is just wide enough for an adult to reach into open-handed.*

2087
03:48:43,000 --> 03:48:52,000
Ryoko: "You sure picked the right well to fall down," Ryoko says with a grim smile. "Like they say, it's always the last place you look."

2088
03:48:52,000 --> 03:49:03,000
*She wastes no time thrusting her hand into the opening. After she feels around for a few seconds, Koji hears the thunk of something solid coming together behind the wall.*

2089
03:49:03,000 --> 03:49:04,000
Koji: "Doctor?"

2090
03:49:04,000 --> 03:49:15,000
*Ryoko pulls her hand out and gives the different-colored stones a gentle push. With the rumble of weights shifting, the stones slide smoothly back into the wall.*

2091
03:49:15,000 --> 03:49:21,000
Ryoko: "So that's how he fooled me. I had no idea this was here the last time I came."

2092
03:49:21,000 --> 03:49:23,000
Koji: "You've been here before?"

2093
03:49:23,000 --> 03:49:34,000
*Koji wants answers, but Ryoko ignores him and peers into the opening. In the beam of her floodlight, Koji can see a concrete tunnel leading into the mountain.*

2094
03:49:34,000 --> 03:49:41,000
Ryoko: "I'm going on ahead, Tonoh. You'd better stay here." Her warning is simple and utterly devoid of warmth.

2095
03:49:41,000 --> 03:49:46,000
*Considering his options, Koji looks from the tunnel to the rope and back again.*

2096
03:49:46,000 --> 03:49:57,000
*He's practically sweating now, thanks to the 190-proof vodka he just drank, but although feeling has returned to his fingers, he still doesn't have the strength to climb.*

2097
03:49:57,000 --> 03:50:02,000
*That said, the thought of being alone in the well again makes him shiver.*

2098
03:50:02,000 --> 03:50:05,000
Koji: "I'll go too. Please take me with you."

2099
03:50:05,000 --> 03:50:07,000
Ryoko: "Heh, have it your way."

2100
03:50:07,000 --> 03:50:13,000
*Ryoko steps into the tunnel without looking back, and Koji doesn't hesitate to follow .*

2101
03:50:13,000 --> 03:50:24,000
Koji: "You were pretty different the last time we met," Koji says sarcastically, following Ryoko as she moves cautiously down the tunnel with her light leading the way.

2102
03:50:24,000 --> 03:50:31,000
Ryoko: "This isn't the hospital, and you're not my patient. This service doesn't come with a smile."

2103
03:50:31,000 --> 03:50:34,000
Koji: "So this is who you really are?"

2104
03:50:34,000 --> 03:50:36,000
Ryoko: "I wonder. Does it matter?"

2105
03:50:36,000 --> 03:50:46,000
*Ryoko suddenly stops and stares at the floor. When Koji looks over her shoulder, he sees a dust-covered rope lying coiled up in the middle of the path.*

2106
03:50:46,000 --> 03:50:47,000
Koji: "What is it?"

2107
03:50:47,000 --> 03:50:51,000
Ryoko: "Something left by the last guy who came down that well."

2108
03:50:51,000 --> 03:50:55,000
*Ryoko picks up the rope, examines it, and hands it to Koji.*

2109
03:50:55,000 --> 03:51:05,000
Ryoko: "It's about twice as long as my rope. It has a knot in it, and both ends have been severed. They were connected before to make a circle."

2110
03:51:05,000 --> 03:51:06,000
Koji: "Huh?"

2111
03:51:06,000 --> 03:51:22,000
Ryoko: "You loop one end of the circle around something topside, then use the rest to climb down into the well. When you're at the bottom, you cut the circle open and pull the whole rope in with you. No trace of your descent is left behind."

2112
03:51:22,000 --> 03:51:29,000
*Ryoko shines her light down the tunnel, revealing that it ends in a closed wooden door about ten meters ahead.*

2113
03:51:29,000 --> 03:51:33,000
Ryoko: "That's how he avoided detection. Really got me good."

2114
03:51:33,000 --> 03:51:36,000
Koji: "You said you've been here before?"

2115
03:51:36,000 --> 03:51:43,000
Ryoko: "Yeah, you and Sakisaka aren't the only ones," Ryoko says dryly. "I checked Ogai's cabin a while back."

2116
03:51:43,000 --> 03:51:49,000
*As Ryoko speaks, she opens her coat and pulls out what she had hanging underneath it.*

2117
03:51:49,000 --> 03:51:54,000
Ryoko: "If there aren't any other exits... then he's still behind that door."

2118
03:51:54,000 --> 03:52:06,000
*At first, Koji thinks that she is holding a steel pipe. Amazed that she would be carrying a weapon, Koji looks closer -- and is appalled when he realizes what it really is.*

2119
03:52:06,000 --> 03:52:07,000
*A gun.*

2120
03:52:07,000 --> 03:52:21,000
*And not one of those sleek handguns that he's seen in the movies, but a double-barreled shotgun. The stock and barrels have been sawed down for easier concealment, enhancing its aura of brutal efficiency.*

2121
03:52:21,000 --> 03:52:22,000
Koji: "What is that!?"

2122
03:52:22,000 --> 03:52:35,000
Ryoko: "A twelve-gauge shotgun," Ryoko replies blandly, as though naming a brand of cigarettes. "I don't have a permit, and cutting it down would be illegal even if I did. Any other questions?"

2123
03:52:35,000 --> 03:52:38,000
Koji: "What are you planning to do with that thing?"

2124
03:52:38,000 --> 03:52:43,000
*Ryoko looks over her shoulder and gives Koji her most chilling smile yet.*

2125
03:52:43,000 --> 03:52:50,000
Ryoko: "When I first learned what Ogai was doing, I was a model citizen. I'd never even gotten a ticket."

2126
03:52:50,000 --> 03:52:59,000
*The woman whom Koji believed was just a normal doctor waves her sawed-off shotgun menacingly as she continues, her tone sharp and bitter.*

2127
03:52:59,000 --> 03:53:04,000
Ryoko: "If I'd had this back then, I could've killed Ogai before he got away.

2128
03:53:04,000 --> 03:53:10,000
Ryoko: "Maybe then none of this would have happened. I feel bad about that, really."

2129
03:53:10,000 --> 03:53:11,000
Koji: "......"

2130
03:53:11,000 --> 03:53:19,000
*Koji listens in silence, helpless to do anything but watch as understanding moves farther and farther out of his grasp.*

2131
03:53:19,000 --> 03:53:32,000
Ryoko: "In other words, everything I do from here on out is to clean up this mess that you and your friends have stepped in. Remember that, and don't ask any unnecessary questions. Got it?"

2132
03:53:32,000 --> 03:53:35,000
*Koji can only nod weakly in response.*

2133
03:53:35,000 --> 03:53:43,000
*With the light in her left hand and the shotgun in her right, Ryoko walks up to the door and takes a deep breath.*

2134
03:53:43,000 --> 03:53:48,000
*Then she kicks the door open, putting her full weight behind the blow.*

2135
03:53:48,000 --> 03:53:58,000
*With a disappointingly feeble sound, the door breaks off of its hinges and falls into the room. Dust billows like white smoke in the beam of Ryoko's light.*

2136
03:53:58,000 --> 03:54:19,000
*The room is large, at least thirty-five meters square. The tiled floor is set with drainage grates, and there's no mistaking the operating table sitting in the middle of the room. Cabinets full of enamelware and drugs line one side of the space, and against the opposite wall stand a writing desk and bookshelves.*

2137
03:54:19,000 --> 03:54:28,000
*Even Koji can recognize that much. The mysterious objects cluttering the tables and shelves, however, are beyond his comprehension.*

2138
03:54:28,000 --> 03:54:43,000
*Mirrors delicately engraved with complex patterns, grotesque statues and masks that must have been left by a race of savages, tapestries woven in nauseating arrays of color, a crystal ball the size of an infant's head...*

2139
03:54:43,000 --> 03:55:03,000
*Any would fetch a hefty price at an antique store, if not for the one thing they all have in common. Every last piece is so loathsome and foul that Koji feels sick just looking at it. It's as though each was designed for the sole sinister purpose of immortalizing its creator's hatred of the world.*

2140
03:55:03,000 --> 03:55:18,000
*Rare-looking books of the sort that he found in Ogai's home are piled here and there, and on one shelf are stacked some scrolls that look to be made of some kind of sheepskin or papyrus -- whatever it is, it's not paper.*

2141
03:55:18,000 --> 03:55:34,000
*Finally, there are the indecipherable chalk patterns and symbols filling every available space on the walls. Even the two sliding blackboards are covered in strange, unreadable scribblings. Just looking at them is making Koji dizzy.*

2142
03:55:34,000 --> 03:55:49,000
Ryoko: "Don't look!" Ryoko snaps at him. "Listen. Don't move, and whatever you do, don't touch anything. Even if something draws your attention, don't look at it. If you see something that feels wrong, stare at your shoes. Got it?"

2143
03:55:49,000 --> 03:55:50,000
Koji: "Y-yeah."

2144
03:55:50,000 --> 03:56:07,000
*Ryoko switches her light's flourescent runners on and sets it on a nearby table where it can illuminate the whole room. She then holsters her shotgun, only to pull out an even more confusing set of tools -- a digital camera and a can of spraypaint.*

2145
03:56:07,000 --> 03:56:26,000
*She gives the can in her left hand a good shake, switches the camera in her right hand on, and steps up to the blackboard while looking at the camera's side-mounted screen. After recording one set of symbols, she covers it with a thick layer of paint, then moves on to the next.*

2146
03:56:26,000 --> 03:56:27,000
Koji: "Um... doctor?"

2147
03:56:27,000 --> 03:56:40,000
Ryoko: "Lesson one. Never look at strange symbols or read anything written in unusual languages like Latin. Use a camera to record them for later examination, then paint over the real thing."

2148
03:56:40,000 --> 03:56:52,000
*Now that she mentions it, Koji realizes that she's only looking at the screen of her camera -- even then, only in short glimpses -- and never directly at any of the drawings.*

2149
03:56:52,000 --> 03:56:57,000
*He understands what she's saying, but it still doesn't make any sense.*

2150
03:56:57,000 --> 03:56:59,000
Koji: "Why do you have to..."

2151
03:56:59,000 --> 03:57:16,000
Ryoko: "Now that you've come this far, you'd better shut up and listen for your own good. Things like crystal balls and mirrors are dangerous. Anything can happen if you break them, so it's best to cover them with a cloth or paint over them for the time being."

2152
03:57:16,000 --> 03:57:21,000
*Koji begins to fear that this doctor might be even crazier than Fuminori.*

2153
03:57:21,000 --> 03:57:28,000
*Despite the burst of energy he received from the vodka, Koji is still exhausted from his night in the well.*

2154
03:57:28,000 --> 03:57:32,000
*The fear is affecting his body, making him dizzy and nauseous.*

2155
03:57:32,000 --> 03:57:39,000
*Soon, the walls are covered in black paint and the stale air is thick with the smell of turpentine.*

2156
03:57:39,000 --> 03:57:47,000
Ryoko: "That should do for now," Ryoko says with relief, then tosses the empty can aside and puts away her video camera.

2157
03:57:47,000 --> 03:57:53,000
Koji: "What happened to Ogai?" Koji asks, supporting himself against a nearby table.

2158
03:57:53,000 --> 03:57:55,000
Ryoko: "Hm? Oh, he was over there."

2159
03:57:55,000 --> 03:58:06,000
*Without stopping her examination of the papers on the writing table, Ryoko points nonchalantly to a Chinese-style screen standing in one corner of the room.*

2160
03:58:06,000 --> 03:58:12,000
*He "was" there. Her clinical choice of tense makes her meaning instantly obvious.*

2161
03:58:12,000 --> 03:58:13,000
Koji: "......"

2162
03:58:13,000 --> 03:58:25,000
*The urge to see for himself is irresistible. Koji staggers across the room to the screen, taking the utmost care not to look at the scaly octopus-thing that is painted on it.*

2163
03:58:25,000 --> 03:58:35,000
*Behind the screen is a large easy chair. Although he's never met the man before, Koji is fairly certain that the person sitting in it is Ogai Masahiko.*

2164
03:58:35,000 --> 03:58:50,000
*Ogai's corpse must have shrunk significantly while drying in this sealed chamber. The body is barely the size of a child's, with only the business suit hanging from the bones offering any hint of Ogai's former stature.*

2165
03:58:50,000 --> 03:58:59,000
*His empty eye sockets and wide-open jaw are filled with darkness -- the same darkness that surrounded Koji at the bottom of the well.*

2166
03:58:59,000 --> 03:59:05,000
*Compared to those gaping voids, the tiny hole in Ogai's right temple is almost demure.*

2167
03:59:05,000 --> 03:59:15,000
*The revolver that he presumably used to kill himself is still clenched in his dangling right hand. It looks like a child's toy compared to Ryoko's shotgun.*

2168
03:59:15,000 --> 03:59:34,000
*Ryoko must have noticed Ogai's corpse while she was spray-painting the walls, and still she kept working without batting an eyelash. Impressive, though not exactly suprising after what he's been through. It's getting difficult to remember the last time he spoke to someone sane.*

2169
03:59:34,000 --> 03:59:45,000
*But if not for her, Koji reminds himself with a bitter smirk, he would have ended up joining this mummified corpse here -- and no one would ever have found him.*

2170
03:59:45,000 --> 03:59:47,000
*Koji's vision suddenly dims.*

2171
03:59:47,000 --> 03:59:52,000
*He's pushed himself too hard, and the Spirytus vodka can't help him anymore.*

2172
03:59:52,000 --> 04:00:03,000
*He collapses to the floor, unable to hang on to his slipping consciousness, and the last thing he sees are Ogai Masahiko's gaping eye sockets staring at him.*

2173
04:00:03,000 --> 04:00:23,000
*When he wakes, Koji finds himself lying on something dry and soft. A bed is a bed, he thinks to himself, even one that smells of mold and dust, and especially after sleeping in cold mud all night. There are no lights hanging from the ceiling, but the soft, warm light of a lamp fills the room.*

2174
04:00:23,000 --> 04:00:33,000
*Simple furnishings, nonexistent decor -- Koji realizes that he's in Ogai's cabin, in the bedroom that he searched before Fuminori pushed him into the well.*

2175
04:00:33,000 --> 04:00:34,000
Ryoko: "You awake?"

2176
04:00:34,000 --> 04:00:47,000
*Ryoko is sitting in a chair against the wall, her expression blank as she studies the pile of documents on the table in front of her. She must have brought them up from Ogai's underground lab.*

2177
04:00:47,000 --> 04:00:52,000
*She turns a page, then takes a bite from the sandwich in her free hand.*

2178
04:00:52,000 --> 04:00:56,000
Ryoko: "If you feel up to eating, there's food over there."

2179
04:00:56,000 --> 04:01:03,000
*Without looking up from the files, she gestures towards the convenience store bag sitting on the nightstand.*

2180
04:01:03,000 --> 04:01:05,000
Koji: "How did I get here?"

2181
04:01:05,000 --> 04:01:13,000
*Koji can't imagine that a woman -- even a woman like Ryoko -- could have climbed out of the well with him on her back.*

2182
04:01:13,000 --> 04:01:43,000
Ryoko: "There was a sealed door behind one of the bookshelves down there," Ryoko mutters, taking care not to let the explanation interfere with her reading or eating. "When I finally got it open, it led to the boiler room underneath the cabin. The other side was hidden with a thin layer of mortar. I figure that's how he got most of his supplies down there. Once he had everything he needed, he could seal it up and use the well instead. Pretty thorough."

2183
04:01:43,000 --> 04:01:47,000
Koji: "Was there really something in there that he needed to hide?"

2184
04:01:47,000 --> 04:01:50,000
Ryoko: "There used to be. This is the last of it."

2185
04:01:50,000 --> 04:01:58,000
*Having finished her sandwich, Ryoko picks up some unsorted papers with her free hand and waves them in the air.*

2186
04:01:58,000 --> 04:02:15,000
Ryoko: "Not all scholars want to get on stage at a symposium and show their research to the world, you know. Some nutcases get their kicks by learning secrets no one else knows, and by being buried with those secrets in hidden tombs that no one'll ever find."

2187
04:02:15,000 --> 04:02:26,000
*Koji still hasn't the slightest idea what Ogai's secret might have been. From what Ryoko said in that tunnel, however, he can guess that Fuminori is somehow involved.*

2188
04:02:26,000 --> 04:02:39,000
Koji: "What happened to Fuminori?" Koji asks desperately, no longer caring who he gets answers from. "What does he have to do with that body down there? Just what is it that you're after?"

2189
04:02:39,000 --> 04:02:51,000
Ryoko: "That's what I'm trying to find out," Ryoko replies coldly, as though Koji's concerns are none of hers. "Sakisaka told me that he was acting on behalf of one of Ogai's relatives."

2190
04:02:51,000 --> 04:02:54,000
Koji: "Yes, he told me the same thing."

2191
04:02:54,000 --> 04:02:57,000
Ryoko: "Oh? Well, at least that's consistent."

2192
04:02:57,000 --> 04:03:02,000
*Ryoko pulls several sheets of looseleaf paper from a different file.*

2193
04:03:02,000 --> 04:03:17,000
Ryoko: "The truth is that Ogai has no relatives. I thought that Sakisaka was simply lying. However, there was another possibility I should have considered. He might have been tricked by someone claiming to be Ogai's family."

2194
04:03:17,000 --> 04:03:20,000
*Ryoko pauses, then looks sidelong at Koji.*

2195
04:03:20,000 --> 04:03:23,000
Ryoko: "Does the name 'Saya' ring a bell?"

2196
04:03:23,000 --> 04:03:25,000
Koji: "Saya? No, who is that?"

2197
04:03:25,000 --> 04:03:31,000
Ryoko: "Who -- or what -- is the question, but the more I read, the less I understand."

2198
04:03:31,000 --> 04:03:36,000
*She sighs bitterly, then returns her attention to the papers in her hand.*

2199
04:03:36,000 --> 04:03:49,000
Ryoko: "All I can say for sure is that it appears to have been the focus of Ogai's research. If Sakisaka is involved with whatever 'Saya' is, then he's already past the point of no return."

2200
04:03:49,000 --> 04:03:54,000
*The icy certainty in Ryoko's voice sends a chill down Koji's spine.*

2201
04:03:54,000 --> 04:03:57,000
Koji: "If so... then what will you do with him?"

2202
04:03:57,000 --> 04:04:01,000
*He has to ask, even though he already knows the answer.*

2203
04:04:01,000 --> 04:04:14,000
Ryoko: "It's like I said," Ryoko replies, smirking at the tension in Koji's voice. "I have no idea how many times I've wished I'd killed Ogai when I had the chance. I won't make the same mistake twice."

2204
04:04:14,000 --> 04:04:17,000
Koji: "If I go to the police, it'll all be over!"

2205
04:04:17,000 --> 04:04:22,000
*Ryoko doesn't respond, as though she didn't even hear what Koji just said.*

2206
04:04:22,000 --> 04:04:29,000
Koji: "Fuminori tried to kill me," Koji continues persistently. "If I press charges, he'll be arrested and..."

2207
04:04:29,000 --> 04:04:44,000
Ryoko: "Ryoko cuts him off harshly. "You have witnesses? Proof? What was Sakisaka's motive? You know, Tonoh, you're completely misunderstanding what the police do. Their job isn't to fight for justice, or even to keep people safe."

2208
04:04:44,000 --> 04:04:46,000
Koji: "W-what are you saying?"

2209
04:04:46,000 --> 04:05:08,000
Ryoko: "Finding reasonable explanations for unreasonable events -- that's what the police are for. They will always choose to believe the simplest, most logical explanation. Just like how water always flows downhill. They aren't interested in the truth. They don't know, or care, that the truth is often stranger than fiction."

2210
04:05:08,000 --> 04:05:12,000
Koji: "Surely they're not all like that! I won't know until I try!"

2211
04:05:12,000 --> 04:05:17,000
Ryoko: "Exactly," Ryoko states, as she pulls another sandwich out of the bag.

2212
04:05:17,000 --> 04:05:27,000
*She hasn't spared Koji a second glance since looking at him earlier. Even while talking, her attention is always focused on the papers in front of her.*

2213
04:05:27,000 --> 04:05:50,000
Ryoko: "Let's say you accuse your friend of pushing you into a well. In addition to your statement, the police will consider two alternate versions of the truth. Maybe you're making it all up to frame your friend. Or -- even simpler -- it was an accident. You fell into the well by yourself, and the shock has made you paranoid or delusional.

2214
04:05:50,000 --> 04:06:03,000
Ryoko: "These three possibilities will compete to see which comes out with the most convincing evidence. No one knows which will be the winner. Are you willing to bet everything you have on your truth?"

2215
04:06:03,000 --> 04:06:04,000
Koji: "......"

2216
04:06:04,000 --> 04:06:06,000
*Koji has no response.*

2217
04:06:06,000 --> 04:06:17,000
*Can he really explain with cold, clear logic what drove Fuminori to do what he did? How can he convince anyone else when he doesn't even understand it himself?*

2218
04:06:17,000 --> 04:06:35,000
